class ActionTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the taxonomy of the Action form of C2 Requirement.

    The taxonomy is a combination of abstract commands, verbs, tasks, etc.
    described in various Joint Publications, training documents for
    operational planning, etc.

    :cvar ADVISE: Counsel and inform of the implications of adopting a
        certain pattern of behavior, beliefs or attitudes.
    :cvar ADVANCE: Conduct offensive operation designed to gain or re-
        establish contact with the enemy.
    :cvar ASSAULT: Climax of an attack; closing with the enemy in hand-
        to-hand fighting.  Short, violent attack, against local
        objective.
    :cvar ASSESS: Pose a judgment after comparing measured performances
        against a standard.
    :cvar ATTACK: Destruction order; orders the destruction of an
        object.
    :cvar ATTACK_ARMED_RECONNAISSANCE: Order the conduct of Aerial
        Reconnaissance in the vicinity of a specified objective, with
        the delivery of ordnance when targets of opportunity are
        located.
    :cvar ATTACK_ASSIGN: Order to prepare to engage or attack an
        objective. Firing is not authorized until ordered or objective
        becomes eligible for destruction under existing doctrine and/or
        Rules of Engagement (ROE).
    :cvar ATTACK_COUNTER: Destruction order; better known as "counter
        attack".  Attack by a part or all of a defending force for such
        specific purposes as regaining ground lost or cutting off or
        destroying adversaries' advance units, with the general
        objective of denying to the adversary the attainment of their
        purpose in attacking.
    :cvar ATTACK_CYBER: Orders attack of an object using cyber
        means/weapons.
    :cvar ATTACK_DEAD: Destruction of Enemy Air Defenses (DEAD).  Order
        the neutralization of enemy air defenses, including radars and
        launchers, in the vicinity of a specific objective through
        physical attack or electronic warfare.
    :cvar ATTACK_DIRECTED_ENERGY: Destruction order; orders the
        destruction of an object using directed energy means/weapons.
    :cvar ATTACK_ELECTRONIC: Also known as EA or Electronic Attack.
        Orders attack of an object using electronic warfare
        means/weapons.
    :cvar ATTACK_KINETIC: Destruction order; orders the destruction of
        an object using kinetic means/weapons.
    :cvar ATTACK_SEAD: Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses (SEAD).  Order
        the neutralization of enemy air defenses, particularly radars,
        in the vicinity of a specific objective using anti-radiation
        weapons or electronic warfare.
    :cvar ATTACK_SWEEP: Order to seek out and destroy enemy entities or
        other targets of opportunity in an allocated area of operations.
    :cvar BREACH: Deliberate or hasty: cross or create a lane through a
        minefield or IED belt or a clear route through a barrier or
        fortification.
    :cvar BREAK_OUT: Continuation of a crossing operation once the force
        has consolidated in the bridgehead; or offensive action by an
        encircled force to link-up with a main force.
    :cvar BUILD_UP: Attain prescribed strength of units and prescribed
        levels of vehicles, equipment, stores and supplies.
    :cvar BYPASS: Move around an obstacle, position or enemy force to
        maintain the momentum of advance.
    :cvar C2: Perform Command and Control (C2) over systems, entities,
        people, etc.  Sibling enumerations include more specific forms
        of C2; use them when applicable.
    :cvar C2_CYBER: Perform Command and Control (C2) over cyber
        functions of systems, entities, people, etc.
    :cvar C2_OPERATIONAL: Perform operational level Command and Control
        (C2) over systems, entities, people, etc.
    :cvar C2_STRATEGIC: Perform strategic level Command and Control (C2)
        over systems, entities, people, etc.
    :cvar C2_TACTICAL: Perform tactical level Command and Control (C2)
        over systems, entities, people, etc.
    :cvar CHARACTERIZE: Develop or maintain information about a
        particular event, thing or other target that is required to
        perform a mission or to satisfy essential elements of
        information (EEI).
    :cvar COLLECT: Assemble, accumulate or acquire data or information.
    :cvar COLLECT_INTEL: Assemble, accumulate or acquire intelligence
        data or information.
    :cvar CONFIRM: Provide current information of previous reporting
        within a specified degree of certainty and/or accuracy.
    :cvar COORDINATE: Bring functions, systems or entities operating in
        the same environment in proper relation in order to avoid
        counter-productive results such as duplication of effort or
        mutually negating actions.
    :cvar CROSS: Deliberate or hasty: pass over or through an obstacle.
    :cvar CROSS_CUE: Preplanned collaborative detection, recognition,
        identification, location or tracking; the deliberate handover of
        a collection/find task to a nominated unit, system or person.
    :cvar DEPLOY: Movement of forces from the current position to the
        operational area. For example, in order to stage for a future
        mission.
    :cvar DISRUPT: Cause tactical havoc to an enemy and is meant for
        assignment to specific operational or tactical actors, targets
        and times.
    :cvar FIND_SEARCH: Search for and find a unit, object, activity,
        situation, event or person or persons.
    :cvar FLASH: Intentionally increase measures of visibility to
        indicate position and/or status.
    :cvar FOLLOW_TO_INFLUENCE: Proximity based show of force to yield a
        behavioral change of an intended target.
    :cvar IDENTIFY: Determine the status (including friendly or hostile
        nature) of the detected unit, object, activity, situation, event
        or person or persons.
    :cvar IDENTIFY_VISUAL: Order the identification of a specified
        objective by visual means.
    :cvar INFORM: Impart information or knowledge.
    :cvar INSERT_INFILTRATE: Deploy reconnaissance, stay-behind or
        raiding forces out of contact with the enemy.
    :cvar INTERDICT: Divert, disrupt, delay or destroy an enemy's
        military potential before it can be used effectively against
        friendly forces.
    :cvar INTERCEPT: Search for and listen to and/or record
        communications and/or electronic data.
    :cvar INTERVENE: Order to turn away a specified target from its
        intended direction of travel.
    :cvar INVESTIGATE_INTERROGATE: Order the collection of additional
        information about a specified objective by sensor or visual
        means.
    :cvar LIAISE: Maintain contact or intercommunication between
        elements of military forces to ensure mutual understanding and
        unity of purpose and action.
    :cvar LINK_UP: Establishment of contact, in enemy controlled
        territory, between one or more friendly units or formations
        which have the same or differing missions.
    :cvar LOCATE_FIX: Establish a position of the detected unit, object,
        activity, situation, event or person or persons to a specified
        accuracy.
    :cvar LOGISTICS: Detailed coordination of a complex operation
        involving many people, facilities, or supplies.  Sibling
        enumerations include more specific forms of logistics; use them
        when applicable.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_LOADING: Logistics focused on loading and unloading
        of items including people and supplies.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_REPLENISH: Logistics focused on replenishing items
        including people and systems.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_RESUPPLY: Logistics focused on resupplying
        consumable items.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_REFUEL: Logistics focused on resupplying of
        consumable energy resources such as fuel.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_TOWING: Logistics focused on movement of items via
        towing.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_TRANSPORT: Logistics focused on movement of items
        via transport.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_TRANSITING: Logistics focused on movement of items.
    :cvar LOGISTICS_SUPPORT: Logistics focused on supporting the needs
        of people, facilities or systems.
    :cvar MANIPULATE: Manage to advantage (person or situation).
    :cvar MANEUVER: Employ forces on the battlefield (using movement) in
        combination with fire or fire potential to achieve a position of
        advantage in respect to the enemy.
    :cvar MARK: Call for fire on a specific location to orient the
        observer or spotter or to indicate targets.
    :cvar MEDEVAC: Medical evacuation (MEDEVAC).  Movement of people to
        facilitate medical assistance.
    :cvar MELD: Transition from an ISR, area search or similar pre-
        engagement action to a target sorting or targeting action
        leading to engagement.
    :cvar MENTOR: Develop capacity through example and/or advice through
        planning and preparation, execution and lessons capture/After
        Action Review (AAR) phases.
    :cvar MONITOR_OBSERVE: Develop or maintain situational awareness,
        pattern of life or atmospherics of a geographical area, activity
        or situation.
    :cvar NONCOMBATANT_OPERATIONS: Operations by people not associated
        with combat or military forces.
    :cvar OCCUPY: Move into and enable proper organization of an area to
        be used as a battle position.
    :cvar ORGANIZE: Give orderly structure to.
    :cvar OTHER: Indicates an other type of Action.  Use of this
        enumerate should avoided or at least minimized.  If used, it
        should only be used temporarily while proposing the addition of
        new well named enumerate(s) to the standard.
    :cvar OVERTHROW: Remove forcibly from power.
    :cvar PATROL: Move tactically within an area of responsibility to
        deliver a clearly defined Effect.  A patrol is conducted in an
        area where an enemy threat precludes normal administrative
        movement.
    :cvar PROCESS_INTEL: Process intelligence in support of operations.
    :cvar PROTECT: 1) To cover or shield from exposure, damage or
        destruction. 2) To keep from harm, attack, injury or
        exploitation. 3) To maintain the status or integrity of. 4)
        Safeguard. 5) Protect by offense, defense or threat of either or
        both. 6) Order to maintain a good posture relative to a
        specified target from which a successful engagement/attack can
        be accomplished if needed.  The standoff distance with respect
        to the target is established by standard operating procedures.
        Also known as COVER.
    :cvar PROTECT_BLOCK: An inherently defensive tactic used to force
        the target to alter course.  For example, force an enemy system
        away from a defended asset or stop its closure.  It is
        accomplished by maneuvering a unit directly in front of the
        closing vessel and maintaining position.  The possibility of
        collision exists, depending on the intent of the closing vessel.
    :cvar PROTECT_CAP: Combat Air Patrol (CAP).  Order to patrol in the
        vicinity of the objective for the purpose of defending against
        hostile aircraft.
    :cvar PROTECT_CAS: Close Air Support (CAS).  Order the delivery of
        ordnance against hostile forces that are in close proximity to
        friendly ground forces. Close coordination with an airborne or
        ground Forward Air Controller (FAC) is required.
    :cvar PROTECT_CCD: Camouflage, concealment and decoys (CCD).  Order
        to protect through the use of CCD.  To mask or conceal from
        detection or viewing.
    :cvar PROTECT_ESCORT: Order to accompany and protect a specified
        objective.
    :cvar PROTECT_KINETIC: Protect using kinetic means/weapons.
    :cvar PROTECT_DIRECTED_ENERGY: Protect using directed energy
        means/weapons.
    :cvar PROTECT_CYBER: Protect using cyber means/weapons.
    :cvar PROTECT_EW: Protect using electronic warfare means/weapons.
    :cvar PROTECT_PICKET: Act as a warning or rescue unit at a point
        outside a formation or geographic area.
    :cvar PROTECT_TOMCAT: Screen returning aircraft to prevent enemy
        aircraft from locating the force.
    :cvar RECONNAISSANCE: Order to obtain intelligence information about
        the objective through the use of sensors or visual means.
    :cvar RETAIN: Maintain occupied location to ensure it's free of
        enemy occupation or use.
    :cvar SEARCH_AND_RESCUE: Order to search for and rescue personnel in
        distress in the vicinity of the objective.
    :cvar SEARCH_AND_RESCUE_COMBAT: Order to search for and rescue
        personnel in distress in the vicinity of active combat.
    :cvar SHADOW: Order to keep a specified target under observation.
        The standoff distance with respect to the target is established
        by standard operating procedures.
    :cvar TARGET: Determines the desired effect and targeting solution
        then obtain required approval to engage/attack.
    :cvar TRACK: Maintain identification and location of a unit,
        activity, situation or person or persons.
    :cvar TRAINING: Train for military missions.
    :cvar WARN: Preplanned provision of information to provide warning
        of a specified situation, event or activity.
    :cvar WITHDRAW: Move away from the enemy (in or out of contact).
    """

    ADVISE = "ADVISE"
    ADVANCE = "ADVANCE"
    ASSAULT = "ASSAULT"
    ASSESS = "ASSESS"
    ATTACK = "ATTACK"
    ATTACK_ARMED_RECONNAISSANCE = "ATTACK_ARMED_RECONNAISSANCE"
    ATTACK_ASSIGN = "ATTACK_ASSIGN"
    ATTACK_COUNTER = "ATTACK_COUNTER"
    ATTACK_CYBER = "ATTACK_CYBER"
