class CharacterizationProductTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    An enumeration of product types that provide information on the
    characteristics (other than position/velocity data) of a target that a
    sensor may produce.

    These include apparent size/signal strength in units such as dBsm, dBW,
    visual magnitude; time series on apparent size; and signal strength
    over select frequency/wavelength bands.

    :cvar POINT_SOI: Short period single measurement of calibrated
        representation of signal amplitude received at sensor. Might be
        per-metric-measurement of visual magnitude or RCS.
    :cvar PER_OBSERVATION_RCS: Point SOI radar cross section on a per-
        reported-metric-measurement basis (may be a tracking-filter
        output measurement rather than single detection-level
        measurement).
    :cvar PER_OBSERVATION_VMAG: Point SOI visual magnitude on a per-
        reported-metric-measurement basis (may be a tracking-filter
        output measurement rather than single detection-level
        measurement)– usually referenced to entry of sensor aperture.
    :cvar AVERAGE_SOI: Calibrated representation of signal amplitude
        received at sensor averaged over a collection period.
    :cvar AVERAGE_RCS: Calibrated representation of radar cross section,
        measured in dBsm, received at sensor and averaged over a
        collection period.
    :cvar AVERAGE_VMAG: Calibrated representation of visual magnitude,
        measured in visual magnitude (log scale), received at sensor and
        averaged over a collection period.
    :cvar AMPLITUDE_VS_TIME: Calibrated representation of signal
        amplitude received at sensor vs time, typically at the same rate
        as used for detection (e.g., pulse rate for a radar or frame
        rate for optical system).
    :cvar NARROWBAND_SOI: RCS vs time, typically at the radar pulse rate
        (but at the pulse-block rate when integrating pulses for
        detection purposes).  Resolution is typically specified in time
        and potentially RCS.
    :cvar HYPERSPECTRAL: Characterization highly resolved in the optical
        spectrum.
    :cvar COLOR_PHOTOMETRY: Magnitude vs time in two or more sub-
        portions of the visible-band spectrum.
    :cvar WIDEBAND_SOI: Radar amplitude vs range characterization where
        the target is resolved in range (due to high-bandwidth of the
        radar pulses).  Can include SOI where target is also resolved in
        Doppler, enabling a radar image in the range and cross-range
        dimensions.
    :cvar RANGE_PROFILE: Wideband SOI with a target resolved in range
        providing range vs amplitude.
    :cvar RANGE_TIME_INTENSITY: Two dimensional plot showing Intensity
        (usually in RCS) of radar scatterers as a function of range and
        time.  Radar scatterers may be multiple targets within radar
        beam or different parts of the same target.
    :cvar DOPPLER_TIME_INTENSITY: Two dimensional plot showing Intensity
        (usually in RCS) of radar scatterers as a function of Doppler
        shift and time.  Radar scatterers may be multiple targets within
        radar beam or different parts of the same target.
    :cvar OPTICAL_IMAGE: Optical image, usually with target resolved in
        the two linear dimensions projected onto a plane perpendicular
        to the line of sight to the target. Resolution is typically
        specified in angular dimensions (millidegrees, arcseconds,
        milliradians).
    :cvar RANGE_DOPPLER_IMAGE: Radar image leveraging wideband
        collections and resolved Doppler differences across elements of
        the target to create a two dimensional image in the dimensions
        of range and cross-range.  Resolution is typically specified in
        meters.
    :cvar IMAGE: Characterization product where the target is resolved
        in at least two linear dimensions, usually with sufficient
        resolution to characterize size through the linear dimensions
        (as opposed to through signal magnitude) and target features.
        Note that sometimes images are used to resolve two closely-
        spaced targets, neither of which is resolved.
    :cvar IR_IMAGE: Image from data in the infrared band, usually with
        target resolved in the two linear dimensions projected onto a
        plane perpendicular to the line of sight to the target.
        Resolution is typically specified in angular dimensions
        (millidegrees, arcseconds, milliradians).
    :cvar IMAGE_3_D: Characterization product with target resolved in
        three linear dimensions.  This may be through processing of
        multiple frames of two-dimensional images or through use of
        sensors capable of simultaneous high-resolution in three
        dimensions (e.g., laser radar with high range-resolution
        combined with high-angular-resolution optics).
    """

    POINT_SOI = "POINT_SOI"
    PER_OBSERVATION_RCS = "PER_OBSERVATION_RCS"
    PER_OBSERVATION_VMAG = "PER_OBSERVATION_VMAG"
    AVERAGE_SOI = "AVERAGE_SOI"
    AVERAGE_RCS = "AVERAGE_RCS"
    AVERAGE_VMAG = "AVERAGE_VMAG"
    AMPLITUDE_VS_TIME = "AMPLITUDE_VS_TIME"
    NARROWBAND_SOI = "NARROWBAND_SOI"
    HYPERSPECTRAL = "HYPERSPECTRAL"
    COLOR_PHOTOMETRY = "COLOR_PHOTOMETRY"
    WIDEBAND_SOI = "WIDEBAND_SOI"
    RANGE_PROFILE = "RANGE_PROFILE"
    RANGE_TIME_INTENSITY = "RANGE_TIME_INTENSITY"
    DOPPLER_TIME_INTENSITY = "DOPPLER_TIME_INTENSITY"
    OPTICAL_IMAGE = "OPTICAL_IMAGE"
    RANGE_DOPPLER_IMAGE = "RANGE_DOPPLER_IMAGE"
    IMAGE = "IMAGE"
    IR_IMAGE = "IR_IMAGE"
    IMAGE_3_D = "IMAGE_3D"


class CharacterizationTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the type of phenomenology used to perform the
    characterization.

    :cvar RF_FREQUENCY: Indicates a measurement of RF Frequency signal
        strength for a specified band.
    :cvar IR_IMAGE: Indicates a collection of infra-red images for a
        specified spectral frequency wavelength range and temperature
        variance.
    :cvar METRIC_OBSERVATIONS: Indicates a collection of metric
        observations to achieve a desired level of resolution.
    :cvar NARROWBAND_SOI: Indicates a collection of the amplitude (in
        decibels) to achieve a desired level of resolution.
    :cvar OPTICAL_IMAGE: Indicates a collection of optical images to
        achieve the desired level of resolution.
    :cvar RCS: Indicates a collection of amplitude resolution
        measurements (in decibels per square meter) to achieve the
        desired level of resolution.
    :cvar VIS_MAG: Indicates a collection of amplitude Resolution
        measurements (measured in meters per pixel) to achieve the
        desired level of resolution.
    :cvar WIDEBAND_SOI: Indicates a collection of the range and cross
        range measurements to achieve the desired level of resolution.
    :cvar PHOTOMETRY: Indicates a collection of visual magnitude
        measurements vs time of target.
    :cvar COLOR_PHOTOMETRY: Indicates a collection of synchronized
        measurements of amplitude vs time of target in three or more
        sub-bands of the visible spectrum.
    """

    RF_FREQUENCY = "RF_FREQUENCY"
    IR_IMAGE = "IR_IMAGE"
    METRIC_OBSERVATIONS = "METRIC_OBSERVATIONS"
    NARROWBAND_SOI = "NARROWBAND_SOI"
    OPTICAL_IMAGE = "OPTICAL_IMAGE"
    RCS = "RCS"
    VIS_MAG = "VIS_MAG"
    WIDEBAND_SOI = "WIDEBAND_SOI"
    PHOTOMETRY = "PHOTOMETRY"
    COLOR_PHOTOMETRY = "COLOR_PHOTOMETRY"


