@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class CollectionParametersType:
    """
    Create a Commanded Timeline Parameters Structure.

    This defines the lower level controls to command as represented in an
    IPI Program command. This version is limited to a single transmit event
    and a single receive event on a single RF channel using event controls.
    It is also limited to a single beampoint used for both transmit and
    receive.

    :ivar collection_parameters_index: Specifies the order of collection
        parameters instead of an implicit assumption that this structure
        is in order.
    :ivar start_pad: Start Pad Duration. Indicates the pad time before
        the start of the first Event Sequence Repetition Interval (ESRI)
        of the collection.
    :ivar end_pad: End Pad Duration. Indicates the pad time after the
        end of the last Event Sequence Repetition Interval (ESRI) of the
        collection.
    :ivar fast_agc_flag: Flag indicating whether Fast AGC is commanded.
    :ivar num_charge_esris: Number of Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI) during Charge part of AGC.
    :ivar num_agc_esris: Number of Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI) during the collection part of AGC. Expected value is zero
        if fastAgcFlag not set.
    :ivar num_set_esris: Number of Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI) during the Set part of AGC. Expected value is zero if
        fastAgcFlag not set.
    :ivar agc_preset_index: Index into table of AGC Presets. Values may
        differ by system.
    :ivar esri_duration: Event Sequence Repetition Interval (ESRI)
        Duration.
    :ivar num_esris: Number of Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI).  Indicates the number of Event Sequence Repetition
        Interval (ESRI) for the collection.
    :ivar rf_channel_index: RF Channel Index.  Indicates the RF Channel
        index to use for the collection.
    :ivar waveform_index: Waveform Index.  Indicates a predefined
        waveform definition used by the commanded Capability.
    :ivar transmit_start_offset: Transmit Start Offset.  Indicates the
        offset from the start of the Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI) to the start of the transmit pulse in system clocks.
    :ivar transmit_length: Transmit Length.Indicates the length of the
        transmit pulse in system clocks.
    :ivar receive_start_offset: Receive Start offset. Indicates the
        offset from the start of the Event Sequence Repetition Interval
        (ESRI) to the start of the receive window.
    :ivar receive_length: Receive Length.Indicates the length of the
        receive window.
    """

