class CommCapabilityEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the first tier in the taxonomy of the Waveform Capability.

    See enumeration annotation for additional details. The enumerates
    aren't necessarily orthogonal. Some enumerates indicate a band while
    others indicate specific communications systems operating within an
    enumerated band.

    :cvar FALCON: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar VALUE_5_G: Indicates communications with the Fifth Generation
        (5G) of mobile technologies; supports high band (also called
        millimeter wave, or MMW), which operates between around 24 and
        300 gigahertz (GHz); mid band, which operates between 1 GHz and
        6 GHz; and low band, which operates below 1 GHz.
    :cvar MBITR: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar AEHF: Indicates the Advanced Extremely High Frequency (AEHF)
        system operated by the United States Space Force, used to relay
        secure communications.
    :cvar JTRS: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar BOWMAN: Indicates the Bowman tactical communications system
        that operates in the HF/VHF/UHF frequency ranges.
    :cvar C_BAND: Indicates communication in the 4-8 GHz frequency range
        i.e. used for satellite communications, for full-time satellite
        TV networks or raw satellite feeds.
    :cvar CDL: Indicates the Common Data Link (CDL), a secure U.S.
        military communications protocol that operates in the KU Band
        and is the primary link/protocol for imagery and signals
        intelligence.
    :cvar CMF: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar DSCS: Indicates the Defense Satellite Communication System, a
        US Space Force satellite constellation.  DSCS is being replaced
        by the Wideband Global SATCOM system.
    :cvar EHF_SATCOM: Indicates extremely high-frequency (EHF) bands
        (30-300 GHz) for broadband transmission over satellite links.
    :cvar EPLRS: Indicates the Enhanced Position Locating Reporting
        System (EPLRS) which provides secure, jam-resistant, near real-
        time data communications support for the five Battlefield
        Functional Areas of the Army Tactical Command and Control System
        (ATCCS).
    :cvar HAVE_QUICK: Indicates the HAVE QUICK radio system which is a
        ECM resistant, frequency-hopping system used to protect
        military aeronautical mobile (OR) radio traffic.
    :cvar HF: Indicates High Frequency (HF) communications in the 3 to
        30 MHz frequency range.
    :cvar HNW: Indicates communication with the Highband Networking
        Waveform (HNW) radio.
    :cvar IFDL: Indicates communications with the Intra-Flight Data Link
        (IFDL).
    :cvar INMARSAT: Indicates communication with the International
        Maritime Satellite (INMARSAT) system which provides marine
        vessels with reliable communications, primarily for enhancement
        of shipping safety.
    :cvar IP: Indicates communications with the Internet Protocol (IP)
        which is the set of rules governing the format of data sent via
        the internet or local network i.e. IPv4 or IPv6.
    :cvar IRIDIUM: Indicates communication using the Iridium
        constellation of 66 crosslinked Low Earth Orbiting (LEO)
        satellites.
    :cvar KA_SATCOM: Indicates satellite communications links operating
        in the 26-40 GHz frequency range.
    :cvar KU_SATCOM: Indicates satellite communications links operating
        in the 12-18 GHz frequency range.
    :cvar L_BAND: Indicates communications in the 1-2 Ghz frequency
        range.  Global Positioning System (GPS) carriers and also
        satellite mobile phones operate in this range.
    :cvar LINK4: Indicates communications with the Link 4 system. Link 4
        is a non-secure military data link for providing vector commands
        to fighter aircraft.  Link4A provides digital surface-to-air,
        air-to-surface, and air-to-air tactical communications.  Link 4C
        is a fighter-to-fighter data link.
    :cvar LINK11: Indicates communications with the Link 11 system. Link
        11 is a secure military tactical data link to exchange digital
        data among airborne, land-based, and shipboard tactical data
        systems. Link 11 is also know as TADIL-A and is compliant with
        MIL-STD-6011.  It will be replaced by Link 22.
    :cvar LINK16: Indicates communications with the Link 16 system
        including via the Joint Range Extension Application Protocol
        (JREAP). Link 16 is a secure military tactical data link
        network. Operates in the frequency band 960–1,215 MHz.  Link 16
        is also known as TADIL-J and is compliant with MIL-STD 6016 and
        STANAG 5516.
    :cvar LINK22: Indicates communications with the Link 22 system.
        Link 22 Is a secure digital Tactical Data Link (TDL) that
        operates in the HF and UHF frequency bands. It was developed to
        securely exchange data between all allied forces (air, ground,
        and sea) and replace Link 11. Link 22 supports both LOS and BLOS
        (Beyond Line of sight) communication links in the HF band.
    :cvar MADL: Indicates communication with the Multifunction Advanced
        Data Link (MADL).
    :cvar MF: Indicates Medium Frequency (MF) communications in the 300
        kilohertz (kHz) to 3 megahertz (MHz) frequency range.
    :cvar MILSTAR: Indicates communication with the Military Strategic
        and Tactical Relay (MILSTAR); a constellation of military
        communications satellites in geosynchronous orbit.
    :cvar MUOS: Indicates communications with the Mobile User Objective
        System (MUOS) constellation of satellites.  Provides global
        narrowband connectivity to terminals, platforms, tactical
        operators and operations centers.
    :cvar S_BAND: Indicates communications in the 2-4 Ghz frequency
        range i.e. WiFi.
    :cvar S_BAND_SATCOM: Indicates communications via satellite in the
        2-4 Ghz frequency range i.e. NASA communication with ISS.
    :cvar SADL: Indicates communications with the Situation Awareness
        Data Link (SADL).
    :cvar SATURN: Indicates communications with the Second Generation
        Anti-Jam Tactical Ultra-High Frequency Radio (SATURN).  SATURN
        operates in the 225-400 MHZ frequency range and will be
        compliant with STANAG-4372 and JIEO-9120A.  It will replace the
        HAVE QUICK II system.
    :cvar SINCGARS: Indicates communications with Single Channel Ground
        and Airborne Radio System (SINCGARS).  SINCGARS operates in the
        30-88 MHz frequency band and will be compliant with MIL-
        STD-188-220 and 241-1/2.
    :cvar SRW: Indicates communications with the Joint Tactical Radio
        System (JTRS) Soldier Radio Waveform (SRW).
    :cvar TCDL: Indicates communications with the Tactical Common Data
        Link (TCDL) radio.
    :cvar TTNT: Indicates communications with the Tactical Targeting
        Network Technology (TTNT) radio.
    :cvar UHF: Indicates communications in the 300 MHz - 3 GHz frequency
        band.
    :cvar UHF_SATCOM: Indicates communications via satellite in the
        240MHz and 270MHz frequency band.
    :cvar VDL: Indicates communications with the VHF Data Link (VDL) or
        VHF Digital Link is a means of sending information between
        aircraft and ground stations.
    :cvar VHF: Indicates Very High Frequency (VHF) communications in the
        30 to 300 MHz frequency range.
    :cvar VLF: Indicates Very Low Frequency (VLF) communications in the
        3 to 30 kHz frequency range.
    :cvar VMF: Indicates communications with the Variable Message Format
        (VMF) protocol.  VMF is compliant MIL-STD-6017.  It is
        a communications protocol used in communicating tactical
        military information.
    :cvar TDRSS: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar FLTSATCOM: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar NCCT: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar VORTEX: No annotation will be provided.
    :cvar WGS: Indicates communications with the Wideband Global SATCOM
        system, a high capacity satellite communications system.
    :cvar WNW: Indicates communications with the Wideband Networking
        Waveform (WNW).
    :cvar X_BAND: Indicates communications via satellite in the 7.25 to
        7.75 GHz  and 7.9 to 8.4 GHz frequency range.  Also known as
        Super High Frequency (SHF) communications.
    :cvar PTW: Indicates communications with the Protected Tactical
        Waveform (PTW).
    :cvar STARLINK: Indicates communications with the Starlink Waveform.
    :cvar OTHER: Indicates another type of Comms.  Use of this enumerate
        should be avoided or at least minimized.  If used, it should
        only be used temporarily while proposing the addition of new
        well named enumerate(s) to the standard.
    """

    FALCON = "FALCON"
    VALUE_5_G = "5G"
    MBITR = "MBITR"
    AEHF = "AEHF"
    JTRS = "JTRS"
    BOWMAN = "BOWMAN"
    C_BAND = "C_BAND"
    CDL = "CDL"
    CMF = "CMF"
    DSCS = "DSCS"
    EHF_SATCOM = "EHF_SATCOM"
    EPLRS = "EPLRS"
    HAVE_QUICK = "HAVE_QUICK"
    HF = "HF"
    HNW = "HNW"
    IFDL = "IFDL"
    INMARSAT = "INMARSAT"
    IP = "IP"
    IRIDIUM = "IRIDIUM"
    KA_SATCOM = "KA_SATCOM"
    KU_SATCOM = "KU_SATCOM"
    L_BAND = "L_BAND"
    LINK4 = "LINK4"
    LINK11 = "LINK11"
    LINK16 = "LINK16"
    LINK22 = "LINK22"
    MADL = "MADL"
    MF = "MF"
    MILSTAR = "MILSTAR"
    MUOS = "MUOS"
    S_BAND = "S_BAND"
    S_BAND_SATCOM = "S_BAND_SATCOM"
    SADL = "SADL"
    SATURN = "SATURN"
    SINCGARS = "SINCGARS"
    SRW = "SRW"
    TCDL = "TCDL"
    TTNT = "TTNT"
    UHF = "UHF"
    UHF_SATCOM = "UHF_SATCOM"
    VDL = "VDL"
    VHF = "VHF"
    VLF = "VLF"
    VMF = "VMF"
    TDRSS = "TDRSS"
    FLTSATCOM = "FLTSATCOM"
    NCCT = "NCCT"
    VORTEX = "VORTEX"
    WGS = "WGS"
    WNW = "WNW"
    X_BAND = "X_BAND"
    PTW = "PTW"
    STARLINK = "STARLINK"
    OTHER = "OTHER"


