class CovarianceMatrixCategoryEnum(Enum):
    """
    Specifies what terms in the covariance matrix are being represented.

    The terms are provided in order of appearance in the lower triangular
    half of the matrix from element 1,1 (item 1) through the last element
    used in the correction. The diagonal terms are the variances of the
    solution parameter, and the off-diagonal terms are the covariances.

    :cvar EQUINOCTIAL: A 6x6 symmetric matrix consisting of 21 values,
        where terms 1-6 represent the following equinoctial elements of
        the solution parameter: Af -- Equinoctial (f) Component of
        Apsidal Vector Ag -- Solstitial (g) Component of Apsidal Vector
        Chi -- CHI Orbit Plane Descriptor Psi -- PSI Orbit Plane
        Descriptor L -- Mean Longitude N -- Mean motion
    :cvar EQUINOCTIAL_PARAMETERS: A 7x7 or larger symmetric matrix
        consisting of 28-120 values, where the equinoctial elements
        (terms 1-6) are followed by one or more additional terms (terms
        7-15) representing the model parameters of the solution:
        Equinoctial Elements: Af -- Equinoctial (f) Component of Apsidal
        Vector Ag -- Solstitial (g) Component of Apsidal Vector Chi --
        CHI Orbit Plane Descriptor Psi -- PSI Orbit Plane Descriptor L
        -- Mean Longitude N -- Mean motion Model Parameters: B -–
        Ballistic Coefficient BDot -– First derivative of Ballistic
        Coefficient Agom –- Radiation Pressure Coefficient T –- Constant
        duration in-track thrust C1, C2...CN –- Optional consider
        parameters Reference developer documentation for the specific
        model parameter terms used and ordering of terms as they vary
        from system to system.
    :cvar MANEUVER_PARAMETERS: A 4x4 symmetric matrix consisting of 10
        values, where terms 1-3 represent the delta velocity and the 4th
        term represents the maneuver start time of the solution
        parameter.
    :cvar POSITION: A 3x3 symmetric matrix consisting of 6 values, where
        the terms represent the position of the solution parameter (ex:
        lat/lon/height, x/y/z)
    :cvar POSITION_VELOCITY: A 6x6 symmetric matrix consisting of 21
        values, where terms 1-3 represent the position and terms 4-6
        represent the velocity of the solution parameter.
    :cvar POSITION_VELOCITY_PARAMETERS: A 7x7 or larger symmetric matrix
        consisting of 28-120 values, where the position and velocity
        (terms 1-6) are followed by one or more additional terms (terms
        7-15) representing the model parameters of the solution.
        Reference developer documentation for the specific model
        parameter terms used and ordering of terms as they vary from
        system to system.
    """

    EQUINOCTIAL = "EQUINOCTIAL"
    EQUINOCTIAL_PARAMETERS = "EQUINOCTIAL_PARAMETERS"
    MANEUVER_PARAMETERS = "MANEUVER_PARAMETERS"
    POSITION = "POSITION"
    POSITION_VELOCITY = "POSITION_VELOCITY"
    POSITION_VELOCITY_PARAMETERS = "POSITION_VELOCITY_PARAMETERS"


