@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class FileHeaderRevAType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar file_security_classification: See simple type documentation.
        REQUIRED FIELD. NITF File Header FSCLAS from ACTDF Overall
        Classification section Classification field. This field shall
        contain a valid value representing the classification level of
        the entire file. Valid values are T (=Top Secret), S (=Secret),
        C (=Confidential), R (=Restricted), U (=Unclassified).
    :ivar file_classification_system: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSCLSY from ACTDF Overall Classification
        section File Security Classification System. This field shall
        contain valid values indicating the national or multinational
        security system used to classify the file. Country Codes per
        FIPS PUB 10-4 shall be used to indicate national security
        systems. The designator "XN" is for classified data generated by
        a component using NATO security system marking guidance. This
        code is outside the FIPS 10-4/GEC document listing, and was
        selected to not duplicate that document's existing codes. If
        this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no
        security classification system applies to the file.  NOTE: If
        FSCLAS is T, S, C, or R, then FSCLSY must be populated with a
        valid code for the security classification system used.  NOTE:
        If any of the following fields are populated with anything other
        than spaces, then FileClassificationSystem (FSCLSY) must be
        populated with a valid code for the security classification
        system used: FSCODE, FSREL, FSDCTP, FSDCDT, FSDCXM, FSDG,
        FSDGDT, FSCLTX, FSCATP, FSCAUT, FSCRSN, FSSRDT, and FSCTLN.
    :ivar file_codewords: See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header FSCODE from ACTDF Overall Classification section File
        Codewords. This field shall contain a valid indicator of the
        security compartments associated with the file. Values include
        zero to four of the digraphs (2 CAP alphas) found in MIL-
        STD-2500x Table A-4, separated by a single ECS space (0x20): The
        selection of a relevant set of codewords is application
        specific. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply
        that no codewords apply to the file.
    :ivar file_control_and_handling: See simple type documentation. NITF
        File Header FSCTLH from ACTDF Overall Classification section
        File Control and Handling. This field shall contain valid
        additional security control and/or handling instructions
        (caveats) associated with the file. Values include one of the
        digraphs found in MIL-STD-2500x Table A-4, where the OTHER
        CODEWORDS row apparently allows other than strictly 2 CAP
        alphas, including ECS-A special characters - that digraph may
        indicate single or multiple caveats. The selection of a relevant
        caveat or caveats is application specific. If this field is all
        ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no additional control and
        handling instructions apply to the file.
    :ivar file_releasing_instructions: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSREL from ACTDF Overall Classification section
        Releasable To. This field shall contain a valid list of country
        and/or multilateral entity codes to which countries and/or
        multilateral entities the file is authorized for release. Valid
        items in the list are one to 7 country codes as found in
        Geopolitical Entities and Codes (GEC) (formerly FIPS PUB 10-4)
        separated by a single ECS space (0x20). If this field is all ECS
        spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no file release instructions
        apply.
    :ivar file_declassification_type: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSDCTP from ACTDF Overall Classification
        section File Declassification Type. This field shall contain a
        valid indicator of the type of security declassification or
        downgrading instructions which apply to the file. Valid values
        are DD (=declassify on a specific date), DE (=declassify upon
        occurrence of an event), GD (=downgrade to a specified level on
        a specific date), GE (=downgrade to a specified level upon
        occurrence of an event), O (=OADR), and X (= exempt from
        automatic declassification). If this field is not present, it
        implies that no file security declassification or downgrading
        instructions apply.
    :ivar file_declassification_date: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSDCDT from ACTDF Overall Classification
        section Declass Date. This field shall indicate the date
        (CCYYMMDD) on which a file is to be declassified if the value in
        File Declassification Type is DD. If this field is all ECS
        spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no file declassification date
        applies.
    :ivar file_declassification_exemption: See simple type
        documentation. NITF File Header FSDCXM from ACTDF Declass
        Exception. This field shall indicate the reason the file is
        exempt from automatic declassification if the value in File
        Declassification Type is X. Valid values are X1 to X8 and X251
        to X259. X1 to X8 correspond to the declassification exemptions
        found in DOD 5200.1-R, paragraphs 4-202b(1) to (8) for material
        exempt from the 10-year rule. X251 to X259 correspond to the
        declassification exemptions found in DOD 5200.1-R, paragraphs
        4-301a(1) to (9) for permanently valuable material exempt from
        the 25-year declassification system. If this field is all ESC
        spaces (0x20), it shall imply that a file declassification
        exemption does not apply.
    :ivar file_downgrade: See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header FSDG from ACTDF Overall Classification section File
        Downgrade. This field shall indicate the classification level to
        which a file is to be downgraded if the values in File
        Declassification Type are GD or GE. Valid values are S
        (=Secret), C (=Confidential), R (=Restricted). If this field
        contains an ECS space (0x20), it shall imply that file security
        downgrading does not apply.
    :ivar file_downgrade_date: See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header FSDGDT from ACTDF Overall Classification section File
        Downgrade Date. This field shall indicate the date (CCYYMMDD) on
        which a file is to be downgraded if the value in File
        Declassification Type is GD. If this field is all ECS spaces
        (0x20), it shall imply that a file security downgrading date
        does not apply.
    :ivar file_classification_text: See simple type documentation. NITF
        File Header FSCLTX from ACTDF Overall Classification section
        File Classification Text. This field shall be used to provide
        additional information about file classification to include
        identification of a declassification or downgrading event if the
        values in File Declassification Type are DE or GE. It may also
        be used to identify multiple classification sources and/or any
        other special handling rules. Values are user defined free text.
        If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that
        additional information about file classification does not
        apply.Note that chars in the range 0xA0 to 0xFF should be
        avoided.
    :ivar file_classification_authority_type: See simple type
        documentation. NITF File Header FSCATP from ACTDF Overall
        Classification section File Classification Authority Type. This
        field indicates the type of authority used to classify the file.
        Valid values are O (= original classification authority), D (=
        derivative from a single source), and M (= derivative from
        multiple sources). If this field contains an ECS space (0x20),
        it implies that file classification authority type does not
        apply.
    :ivar file_classification_authority: File Classification Authority
        aka File Classified By. See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header FSCAUT from ACTDF Overall Classification section
        Classified By. This field shall identify the classification
        authority for the file dependent upon the value in File
        Classification Authority Type. Values are user defined free text
        which should contain the following information: original
        classification authority name and position or personal
        identifier if the value in File Classification Authority Type is
        O; title of the document or security classification guide used
        to classify the file if the value in File Classification
        Authority Type is D; and Derive-Multiple if the file
        classification was derived from multiple sources and the value
        of the FSCATP field is M. In the latter case, the file
        originator will maintain a record of the sources used in
        accordance with existing security directives. One of the
        multiple sources may also be identified in File Classification
        Text if desired. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it
        shall imply that no file classification authority applies.
    :ivar file_classification_reason: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSCRSN from ACTDF Overall Classification
        section File Classification Reason. This field contains values
        indicating the reason for classifying the file. Valid values are
        A to G. These correspond to the reasons for original
        classification per E.O. 12958, Section 1.5.(a) to (g). If this
        field contains an ASCII space (0x20), it means that no file
        classification reason applies.
    :ivar file_security_source_date: See simple type documentation. NITF
        File Header FSSRDT from ACTDF Overall Classification section
        File Security Source Date in form CCYYMMDD. This field shall
        indicate the date of the source used to derive the
        classification of the file. In the case of multiple sources, the
        date of the most recent source shall be used. If this field is
        all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that a file security
        source date does not apply.
    :ivar file_security_control_number: See simple type documentation.
        NITF File Header FSCTLN from ACTDF Overall Classification
        section File Security Control Number. This field shall contain a
        valid security control number associated with the file. The
        format of the security control number shall be in accordance
        with the regulations governing the appropriate security channel
        or channels. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall
        imply that no file security control number applies.
    :ivar originators_name: See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header ONAME from ACTDF Originator. This field shall contain a
        valid name for the operator who originated the file. If the
        field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall represent that no
        operator is assigned responsibility for origination.
    :ivar originators_phone: See simple type documentation. NITF File
        Header OPHONE from ACTDF Originator Phone Number. Default is all
        spaces if not extant in ACTDF. This field shall contain a valid
        phone number for the operator who originated the file. If the
        field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall represent that no phone
        number is available for the operator assigned responsibility for
        origination.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "FileHeaderRevA_Type"

