class FileTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the content of the file.

    :cvar ACO: Indicates the product is Airspace Control Order – MIL-
        STD-6040 – US Message Text Format (MTF).
    :cvar ACTDF: Indicates the product is Airspace Collection Tasking
        Data Format.
    :cvar ATO: Indicates a product containing Airspace Tasking Order –
        MIL-STD-6040 – US Message Text Format (MTF).
    :cvar RSTA: Air Tasking Order - Reconnaissance, Surveillance, and
        Target Acquisition.
    :cvar BIT_REPORT: Indicates a file that is an output of a built-in-
        test (BIT).
    :cvar CALIBRATION_REPORT: Indicates a file that is an output of a
        calibration.
    :cvar FAULT_LOG: Indicates a file that contains fault records.
    :cvar TEST_INSTRUMENTATION_LOG: Indicates a file that contains a log
        of test instrumentation resulting from the TEST_INSTRUMENTATION
        Subsystem setting.  See SubsystemSettingsCommand message for
        further details.
    :cvar DATA_RECORDING_LOG: Indicates a file that contains a log of
        data recording resulting from the DATA_RECORDING Subsystem
        setting.  See SubsystemSettingsCommand message for further
        details.
    :cvar DEBUG_REPORTING_LOG: Indicates a file that contains a log of
        debug data resulting from the DEBUG_REPORTING Subsystem setting.
        See SubsystemSettingsCommand message for further details.
    :cvar SUBSYSTEM_STREAM_LOG: Indicates a file that contains a log of
        SubsystemStream message data resulting from a Subsystem setting.
        See SubsystemSettingsCommand and SubsystemStream messages for
        further details.
    :cvar UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE: Indicates a file that contains
        data required for a Service, Subsystem, Capability, Component,
        etc. to learn its identity as a UCI network node.  UCI node
        configuration data is one of several categories of data that may
        be needed for a given Service, Subsystem, Capability, Component,
        etc. to reach an operational/available state.  Other categories
        are INITIALIZATION_DATA, MDF and SUBSYSTEM_OFP.
    :cvar INITIALIZATION_DATA: Indicates a file that contains
        initialization data for a Service, Subsystem, Capability,
        Component, etc.  Initialization data is one of several
        categories of data that may be needed for a given Service,
        Subsystem, Capability, Component, etc. to reach an
        operational/available state.  Other categories are
        UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE, MDF and SUBSYSTEM_OFP.
    :cvar MDF: Indicates a Mission Data File (MDF) for a Service,
        Subsystem, Capability and/or Component.  MDF data is one of
        several categories of data that may be needed for a given
        Service, Subsystem, Capability, Component, etc. to reach an
        operational/available state.  Other categories are
        UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE, INITIALIZATION_DATA and
        SUBSYSTEM_OFP. This can include items such as Common Route
        Definition (CRD) and Electronic Order of Battle (EOB) files.
    :cvar SUBSYSTEM_OFP: Indicates a file containing a Subsystem
        Operational Flight Program (OFP).  SUBSYSTEM_OFP data is one of
        several categories of data that may be needed for a given
        Service, Subsystem, Capability, Component, etc. to reach an
        operational/available state.  Other categories are
        UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE, INITIALIZATION_DATA and MDF.
    :cvar CHECKPOINT_FILE: Indicates a file that contains checkpoint
        data.
    :cvar MAINTENANCE_LOG: Indicates a file that contains maintenance
        log data.
    :cvar SOD: Space Operations Directive captures Joint Force Space
        Component Commander's (JFSCC) guidance and intent. Conveys
        prioritization and apportionment guidance focused on the
        applicable execution period.
    :cvar MSP: Master Space Plan. Allocates resources to each desired
        effect and serves as the source to generate unit tasking and
        coordination within the Joint Space Tasking Order (JSTO) and
        Special Instructions (SPINS).
    :cvar JIPTL: Joint Integrated Prioritized Target List. Highest
        prioritized targets of each component.
    :cvar JSTO: Joint Space Tasking Order. Transmits JFSCC's guidance
        and priorities for a short-duration time frame, assigns tasks to
        meet operational objectives, and, when required, synchronizes
        and integrates JFSCC activities with other Combatant Command
        (CCMD) operations.
    :cvar PLAN_ORD: Planning Order. Planning directive providing
        essential planning guidance and directs the initiation of plan
        development before the directing authority approves a military
        Course of Action (COA).
    :cvar OP_ORD: Operation Order. Directive issued by a commander to
        subordinate commanders for the purpose of effecting the
        coordinated execution of an operation.
    :cvar WARN_ORD: Warning Order.  Issued by the Chairman of the Joint
        Chiefs of Staff (CJCS), is a planning directive that initiates
        the development and evaluation of military COAs by a supported
        commander.
    :cvar DEPLOYMENT_ORD: Deployment Order. Planning directive from
        SecDef, issued by the CJCS, that authorizes and directs the
        transfer of forces between CCMDs by reassignment or attachment.
        A deployment / redeployment order normally specifies the
        authority that the gaining Combatant Commander (CCDR) will
        exercise over the transferred forces.
    :cvar ALERT_ORD: Alert Order. Planning directive providing essential
        planning guidance and directs the initiation of plan development
        after the directing authority approves a military COA.
    :cvar FRAG_ORD: Fragmentary Order. Address specific changes to the
        Operation Order (OPORD) without restating complete OP_ORD.
    :cvar EX_ORD: Execute Order. Directive to implement an approved
        military CONOPS.
    :cvar SPINS: Special Instructions. Provide operational and tactical
        direction and approved operational procedures. This can include
        items such as Crew Member Mission Planning Products (CMMPP).
    :cvar COMMANDERS_INTENT: Commanders Intent.  Succinctly describes
        what constitutes success for the operation. Includes the
        operation's purpose, key tasks, and the conditions that define
        the end state. Links the mission, concept of operations, and
        tasks to subordinate units.
    :cvar ORBITAL_DEBRIS: Indicates a file that contains orbital debris
        estimation data.
    :cvar CAD: Computer Aided Design.  CAD file is a digital file format
        of an object generated and used by a CAD software. Each CAD
        system has its own method of describing geometry, both
        mathematically and structurally. CAD files hold information for
        these processes, as well as drafting information.
    :cvar CONSTRAINT_SCORE_REPORT: Indicates a file that contains
        constraint scoring data.
    :cvar SAIF: Indicates a file that contains Shared Aperture
        Information.
    :cvar OTHER: Indicates the content of the file does not fall into
        any of the other categories.  Recommended for restricted use for
        pending change package proposals or debug purposes.
    """

    ACO = "ACO"
    ACTDF = "ACTDF"
    ATO = "ATO"
    RSTA = "RSTA"
    BIT_REPORT = "BIT_REPORT"
    CALIBRATION_REPORT = "CALIBRATION_REPORT"
    FAULT_LOG = "FAULT_LOG"
    TEST_INSTRUMENTATION_LOG = "TEST_INSTRUMENTATION_LOG"
    DATA_RECORDING_LOG = "DATA_RECORDING_LOG"
    DEBUG_REPORTING_LOG = "DEBUG_REPORTING_LOG"
    SUBSYSTEM_STREAM_LOG = "SUBSYSTEM_STREAM_LOG"
    UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE = "UCI_NODE_CONFIGURATION_FILE"
    INITIALIZATION_DATA = "INITIALIZATION_DATA"
    MDF = "MDF"
    SUBSYSTEM_OFP = "SUBSYSTEM_OFP"
    CHECKPOINT_FILE = "CHECKPOINT_FILE"
    MAINTENANCE_LOG = "MAINTENANCE_LOG"
    SOD = "SOD"
    MSP = "MSP"
    JIPTL = "JIPTL"
    JSTO = "JSTO"
    PLAN_ORD = "PLAN_ORD"
    OP_ORD = "OP_ORD"
    WARN_ORD = "WARN_ORD"
    DEPLOYMENT_ORD = "DEPLOYMENT_ORD"
    ALERT_ORD = "ALERT_ORD"
    FRAG_ORD = "FRAG_ORD"
    EX_ORD = "EX_ORD"
    SPINS = "SPINS"
    COMMANDERS_INTENT = "COMMANDERS_INTENT"
    ORBITAL_DEBRIS = "ORBITAL_DEBRIS"
    CAD = "CAD"
    CONSTRAINT_SCORE_REPORT = "CONSTRAINT_SCORE_REPORT"
    SAIF = "SAIF"
    OTHER = "OTHER"


