class LosMeasurementEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the reference for pointing of a Capability.

    For example, for an AMTI Capability this enum would indicate whether
    the AMTI scan volume is pointed relative to the System body or along a
    fixed inertial angle.

    :cvar BODY: Indicates body frame.  The body coordinate frame axes is
        an orthogonal triad of axes X, Y, and Z with an origin fixed at
        the location determined to be optimal for the platform.  The
        x-axis is positive in the forward direction of the vehicle (e.g.
        aircraft nose).  The y-axis is positive to the right of the
        forward direction of the vehicle (e.g. aircraft right wing).
        The z-axis is positive down through the vehicle.  The platform
        body coordinate system with respect to the NED coordinate system
        is described through the platform pitch, roll, and yaw Euler
        angles.
    :cvar NED: The NED coordinate system is a geographic frame with its
        origin at a defined point on the platform, generally the
        mounting point of an inertial system.  The NED coordinate frame
        is a North, East, Down frame: Down is normal to the WGS-84
        reference ellipsoid, North points to the North pole, which is in
        the direction of the earth's inertial angular velocity projected
        onto the local horizontal plane, and East completes the
        orthogonal coordinate system.
    :cvar INERTIAL: The inertial coordinate system differs from the NED
        coordinate system by WanderAngle.  If WanderAngle is not
        provided or is zero, then the inertial coordinate frame is the
        NED coordinate frame.
    :cvar CAPABILITY: The Capability reference frame is defined with
        respect to the subsystem (or component) that is providing the
        associated Capability. This allows the LOS to be defined in the
        natural coordinate system of the element providing the
        Capability. For example the rows and columns of the focal plane
        of an optical system providing a PO Capability could be used.
        Depending upon the use case, offsets and angles that define the
        orientation of this frame can be described by the
        InstallationDetails in the SubsystemConfiguration and
        ComponentConfiguration messages and/or LOS defined in associated
        Activity, Capability, Command messages. Care must be taken to
        avoid circular references since the LOS_ReferenceFrame
        enumerations are options in many of these messages.
    :cvar ARRAY_FRAME: The array reference frame is defined with respect
        to the boresight of the sensor.
    """

    BODY = "BODY"
    NED = "NED"
    INERTIAL = "INERTIAL"
    CAPABILITY = "CAPABILITY"
    ARRAY_FRAME = "ARRAY_FRAME"


