class MissionPlanningByCaseTriggerEnum(Enum):
    """
    Enumeration of the initial "by case" triggers for autonomous mission
    planning functions.

    :cvar CAPABILITY_ADDED: This trigger refers to a new Capability
        which becomes available or a previously failed Capability which
        has been restored.
    :cvar CAPABILITY_FAILURE: This trigger refers to a failure of a
        Capability or supporting Capability needed to perform some task
        planned for the future.
    :cvar COMMS_LOST: This trigger refers to lost comms.
    :cvar DMPI_OVER_DESIGNATION: This trigger refers to a situation
        where the designated DMPIs exceed those initially reserved for
        the Task, if this creates a shortage for other assigned Tasks.
    :cvar DMPI_UNDER_DESIGNATION: This trigger refers to a situation
        where the designated DMPIs are less than those initially
        reserved for the task, and if weapons not designated can be used
        to perform previous unallocated tasks.
    :cvar ENDURANCE_LOW: This trigger refers to a low remaining
        endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power.
    :cvar OFF_ROUTE: This trigger refers to a vehicle that has deviated
        from the planned route to such a degree that a replan is
        required.
    :cvar PROXIMITY_CONFLICT: This trigger refers to the proximity of
        two items (Systems, Entities or other items) that exceeded a
        minimum geospatial separation limit as specified in OpRouting
        messages.
    :cvar RELEASE_POINT_OUTSIDE_LAR: This trigger refers to the location
        of a DMPI, updated LAR calculations or other changes that have
        resulted in the planned release point for a weapon falling
        outside the weapon LAR.
    :cvar ROUTE_CONFLICT: This trigger refers to a route that exceeded a
        minimum geospatial separation limit with another item or items.
        The separation is between a planned/navigated route and other
        routes or conflicting items as specified in OpRouting messages.
    :cvar ROUTE_VULNERABILITY: This trigger refers to a pop-up threat
        which is in conflict with an existing plan.
    :cvar SYSTEM_STATE_CHANGE: This trigger refers to a system state
        change as indicated by the SystemStatus message.
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_ADDED: This trigger indicates whether or not
        allocation/replanning due to a new Requirement is allowed.
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_DEPENDENCY_FAILED: This trigger refers to a
        vehicle that cannot perform a Requirement because it is
        dependent on a Requirement that failed or otherwise cannot be
        planned/executed.
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_DROPPED: This trigger refers to a Requirement
        execution state transition to DROPPED, as indicated by execution
        status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus,
        etc.).
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_FAILED: This trigger refers to a Requirement
        execution state transition to FAILED, as indicated by execution
        status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus,
        etc.).
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_CHANGE: This trigger refers to a change to a
        Requirement that impacts an existing plan.  For example, a
        change of the position of the target of the Requirement.
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_TIMING: This trigger a Requirement that is not
        expected to meet its timing constraints.
    :cvar ZONE_VIOLATION: This trigger refers to an OpZone conflicts
        with the current plan.
    :cvar SPACECRAFT_PROXIMITY_CONFLICT: This trigger refers to the
        proximity of two spacecraft (Systems, Entities or other space
        items) that exceeded a minimum geospatial separation limit.
        Monitoring for this trigger should be based on current position
        of live items, not planned/predicted/propagated positions of
        Systems; see sibling OrbitConflict element.
    :cvar ORBIT_CONFLICT: This trigger refers to the position along a
        future planned/predicted/propagated orbit for a spacecraft
        exceeding a minimum geospatial separation limit with another
        item or items.
    :cvar OFF_PLANNED_ORBIT: This trigger refers to a spacecraft that
        has deviated from its planned orbit to such a degree that a
        replan is required.
    :cvar SPACECRAFT_ENDURANCE_LOW: This trigger refers to a low
        remaining endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power.
    :cvar RESPONSE_PLAN: This trigger refers to planning as a result of
        a Response or ResponsePlan.
    """

    CAPABILITY_ADDED = "CAPABILITY_ADDED"
    CAPABILITY_FAILURE = "CAPABILITY_FAILURE"
    COMMS_LOST = "COMMS_LOST"
    DMPI_OVER_DESIGNATION = "DMPI_OVER_DESIGNATION"
    DMPI_UNDER_DESIGNATION = "DMPI_UNDER_DESIGNATION"
    ENDURANCE_LOW = "ENDURANCE_LOW"
    OFF_ROUTE = "OFF_ROUTE"
    PROXIMITY_CONFLICT = "PROXIMITY_CONFLICT"
    RELEASE_POINT_OUTSIDE_LAR = "RELEASE_POINT_OUTSIDE_LAR"
    ROUTE_CONFLICT = "ROUTE_CONFLICT"
    ROUTE_VULNERABILITY = "ROUTE_VULNERABILITY"
    SYSTEM_STATE_CHANGE = "SYSTEM_STATE_CHANGE"
    REQUIREMENT_ADDED = "REQUIREMENT_ADDED"
    REQUIREMENT_DEPENDENCY_FAILED = "REQUIREMENT_DEPENDENCY_FAILED"
    REQUIREMENT_DROPPED = "REQUIREMENT_DROPPED"
    REQUIREMENT_FAILED = "REQUIREMENT_FAILED"
    REQUIREMENT_CHANGE = "REQUIREMENT_CHANGE"
    REQUIREMENT_TIMING = "REQUIREMENT_TIMING"
    ZONE_VIOLATION = "ZONE_VIOLATION"
    SPACECRAFT_PROXIMITY_CONFLICT = "SPACECRAFT_PROXIMITY_CONFLICT"
    ORBIT_CONFLICT = "ORBIT_CONFLICT"
    OFF_PLANNED_ORBIT = "OFF_PLANNED_ORBIT"
    SPACECRAFT_ENDURANCE_LOW = "SPACECRAFT_ENDURANCE_LOW"
    RESPONSE_PLAN = "RESPONSE_PLAN"


