class NavigationCapabilityEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates how the Navigation Capability can be initiated.

    :cvar MISSION_PLAN_NAVIGATION: Navigation by Mission Plan declares
        the system is able to be commanded to navigate to certain points
        of a Mission Plan.
    :cvar FIXED_POSITION_NAVIGATION: Navigation by a fixed position
        declares the system is able to be commanded to navigate to
        certain geospatial point. An example could be commanding a
        system to navigate to an OpPoint or specific line.
    :cvar SLAVED_NAVIGATION: Navigation by slaving to an object declares
        the system is able to be commanded to navigate to a geospatial
        object and to maintain that navigational contract even when the
        object becomes kinetic in nature. An example could be commanding
        a system to navigate to an Entity that is static at a facility
        but becomes kinetic when the commanded system begins its
        transit. The expectation is that the system will continue to
        navigate to the entiry regardless of movement.
    :cvar MANUAL_NAVIGATION: Navigation by manual control declares the
        system is able to be commanded to navigate by means of local
        operator (i.e pilot, tank commander, boat captain, etc.).
        Because of the nature of this capability (uncommandable
        capability), further inclusion of ManualNavigation is not seen
        in the majority of the Navigation family of messages.
    :cvar AUTOPILOT_NAVIGATION: Navigation by auto pilot declares the
        system is able to be commanded to navigate through means of
        traditional auotpilot modes. Examples are altitude, airspeed,
        and heading hold.
    :cvar OWNSHIP_NAVIGATION: Navigation by ownship declares the system
        is able to be commanded to navigate by means of advanced
        autonomy. Examples of ownship navigation are swarm and team
        navigational capabilities.
    :cvar LOITER_NAVIGATION: Navigation by loiter declares the system is
        able to be commanded to navigate to certain geospatial point and
        commence a loiter pattern. An example could be commanding a
        system to navigate to a geospatial point and commence a
        racetrack loiter.
    :cvar OTHER: Navigational capabilities other than what is currently
        listed.
    """

    MISSION_PLAN_NAVIGATION = "MISSION_PLAN_NAVIGATION"
    FIXED_POSITION_NAVIGATION = "FIXED_POSITION_NAVIGATION"
    SLAVED_NAVIGATION = "SLAVED_NAVIGATION"
    MANUAL_NAVIGATION = "MANUAL_NAVIGATION"
    AUTOPILOT_NAVIGATION = "AUTOPILOT_NAVIGATION"
    OWNSHIP_NAVIGATION = "OWNSHIP_NAVIGATION"
    LOITER_NAVIGATION = "LOITER_NAVIGATION"
    OTHER = "OTHER"


