class PlanningDataSourceEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates category/type of source for data to use for planning.

    :cvar LIVE: Indicates live position and status data should be used
        as the basis of planning for a given System.  Live position and
        status data is given in the "station-keeping" set of UCI
        messages including PositionReport/SystemOrbitalPositionReport,
        SystemStatus, NavigationReport, [Capability]Status and
        [Capability]Activity.
    :cvar NON_LIVE: Indicates non-live position and status data should
        be used as the basis of planning for a given System.  Non-live
        position and status data is given in the SystemReadiness
        message.
    :cvar CONTEXT: Indicates the choice between live vs. non-live
        position and status data should be made based on context.  When
        a *PlanCommand initiates planning for a particular Mission, the
        planning Service should use live data (as described in the
        sibling LIVE enumerate) if the associated Mission message
        indicates the Mission is active, the given System has activated
        and reached the initial conditions of the existing Plan for that
        Mission and the given System is reporting live "station-keeping"
        messages.  Otherwise, non-live data (as described in the sibling
        NON_LIVE enumerate should be used.
    """

    LIVE = "LIVE"
    NON_LIVE = "NON_LIVE"
    CONTEXT = "CONTEXT"


class PlanningInterfaceEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates categories of messages sets used for planning.

    :cvar PLAN_COMMAND: Indicates *PlanCommand messages as an interface.
        A System that supports *PlanCommand messages as an interface can
        be invoked to create *Plans.  Note: SupportPlans series of
        messages do not fall under the PLAN_COMMAND interface, they use
        the SupportPlanRequest* messages instead.
    :cvar PLAN_VALIDATION: Indicates *PlanValidation messages as an
        interface.  A System that supports *PlanValidation messages can
        be invoked to validate an existing *Plan.  Note: SupportPlans
        series of messages do not fall under the PLAN_VALIDATION
        interface, they use the SupportManagement* messages are used
        instead.
    :cvar AUTOMATED_PLANNING: Indicates various messages as a triggering
        interface for autonomous/automated planning.  This enumerate is
        a self-invoked version of the sibling PLAN_COMMAND enumerate.
        There are many enumerated triggers (and associated messages) as
        indicated in the PlanningFunction* messages.   A System that
        supports automated planning as an interface supports
        configuration (enable/disable) of its automated planning
        triggers via the PlanningFunction* messages.
    :cvar REQUIREMENT_MANAGEMENT: Indicates an interface for assignment
        of Requirement planning responsibility using the RequirementSet
        message.
    :cvar PLAN_SCORES: Indicates a Plan Score interface.  A System that
        supports a Plan Score interface can be invoked to score an
        existing *Plan.
    :cvar PLAN_METRICS: Indicates a Plan Metrics interface.  A System
        that supports a Plan Metrics interface can be invoked to
        calculate metrics for an existing *Plan.
    :cvar PLAN_ASSESSMENT: Indicates a Plan Assessment interface.  A
        System that supports a Plan Assessment interface can be invoked
        to assess an existing *Plan.
    """

    PLAN_COMMAND = "PLAN_COMMAND"
    PLAN_VALIDATION = "PLAN_VALIDATION"
    AUTOMATED_PLANNING = "AUTOMATED_PLANNING"
    REQUIREMENT_MANAGEMENT = "REQUIREMENT_MANAGEMENT"
    PLAN_SCORES = "PLAN_SCORES"
    PLAN_METRICS = "PLAN_METRICS"
    PLAN_ASSESSMENT = "PLAN_ASSESSMENT"


class PlanningResultEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the results of allocation planning for a Requirement.

    :cvar ALLOCATED: Indicates the Requirement was in the list of
        Requirements in a *PlanCommand and was successfully allocated to
        a System.  For example, a Task in TaskPlanCommand (listed by
        TaskID and/or through a reference to a superior TaskPlan) that
        was successfully allocated to a candidate System.
    :cvar REALLOCATED_SAME_SYSTEM: Indicates the Requirement was
        allocated in an existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand
        and remains allocated to the same candidate  in the new *Plans
        produced by the *PlanCommand.  For example, a Task that was
        previously allocated in a candidate's constraining plan remains
        in the same candidate's new TaskPlan.
    :cvar REALLOCATED_NEW_SYSTEM: Indicates the Requirement was
        allocated in an existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand
        but is allocated to a different System in the new *Plans
        produced by the *PlanCommand.  For example, a Task that was
        previously allocated in a candidate's constraining plan could be
        out prioritized by new Tasks and shifted to a different
        candidate's  TaskPlan.
    :cvar UNALLOCATED: Indicates the Requirement was in the list of
        Requirements in a *PlanCommand and was not successfully
        allocated to a System.  For example, a Task in TaskPlanCommand
        (listed by TaskID and/or through a reference to a superior
        TaskPlan) that was not successfully allocated.
    :cvar DEALLOCATED: Indicates the Requirement was allocated in an
        existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand but was is no
        longer allocated in the new *Plans produced by the *PlanCommand.
        For example, a Task that was previously allocated in a
        candidate's constraining plan could be out prioritized by new
        Tasks and no longer allocated in any candidate's  TaskPlan.
    :cvar PLANNED: Indicates the Requirement was planned in a
        *ActivityPlan.
    """

    ALLOCATED = "ALLOCATED"
    REALLOCATED_SAME_SYSTEM = "REALLOCATED_SAME_SYSTEM"
    REALLOCATED_NEW_SYSTEM = "REALLOCATED_NEW_SYSTEM"
    UNALLOCATED = "UNALLOCATED"
    DEALLOCATED = "DEALLOCATED"
    PLANNED = "PLANNED"


