class SensingTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    An enumeration specifying types of sensing used to characterize the
    environment via observation, measurement, collection or similar means.

    :cvar ACOUSTIC: Measurement, collection or other sensing of sound
        levels.
    :cvar AIR_SAMPLE: Sensing of air to determine the presence or
        characteristics of gases, molecules or other materials in it.
    :cvar BIOLOGICAL: Sensing to determine the presence or
        characteristics of biological materials.
    :cvar CHEMICAL: Sensing to determine the presence or characteristics
        of chemical materials.
    :cvar CONTRAIL: Sensing to determine the presence or characteristics
        of aircraft contrails.
    :cvar EOIR: Measurement, collection or other sensing of optical or
        infrared emissions or reflections.  Sibling enumerations provide
        more specific forms of EO/IR sensing; use them when applicable.
    :cvar EOIR_FIRE_CONTROL: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        optical or infrared emissions or reflections for the purpose of
        controlling a weapon via a datalink or other communications
        channel.
    :cvar EOIR_IMAGING: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        optical or infrared emissions or reflections for the purpose of
        creating imagery.
    :cvar EOIR_TARGETING: Use of a laser or other active optical or
        infrared device to illuminate a target for activities such as
        sensor pointing or weapon guidance via a seeker on the weapon or
        point.  Targeting can be similar to fire control depending on
        the weapon type.
    :cvar EOIR_TRACKING: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        optical or infrared emissions or reflections for the purpose of
        determining the location of an object.
    :cvar EOIR_VIDEO: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        optical or infrared emissions or reflections for the purpose of
        creating video.
    :cvar EYESIGHT: Observation via human eyesight.
    :cvar GEOINT: Geospatial intelligence (GEOINT) is intelligence about
        the human activity on earth derived from the exploitation and
        analysis of imagery and geospatial information that describes,
        assesses, and visually depicts physical features and
        geographically referenced activities on the Earth.
    :cvar HUMINT: Human intelligence (HUMINT) is intelligence gathered
        by means of interpersonal contact, as opposed to the more
        technical intelligence gathering disciplines such as signals
        intelligence, imagery intelligence and measurement and signature
        intelligence.
    :cvar IMINT: Imagery intelligence (IMINT) is an intelligence
        gathering discipline wherein imagery is analyzed to identify
        information of intelligence value.
    :cvar MAGNETIC_ANOMALY: Detection or measurement of an object based
        on the object's effect on the local electromagnetic field.
    :cvar MASINT: Measurement and signature intelligence (MASINT) is a
        technical branch of intelligence gathering, which serves to
        detect, track, identify or describe the distinctive
        characteristics of fixed or dynamic target sources.
    :cvar NUCLEAR: Sensing to detect nuclear explosions, nuclear
        materials or other characteristics of nuclear weapons.
    :cvar OTHER: Indicates another type of sensing.  Use of this
        enumerate should avoided or at least minimized.  If used, it
        should only be used temporarily while proposing the addition of
        new well named enumerate(s) to the standard.
    :cvar RADAR: Measurement, collection or other sensing of radar
        emissions or reflections.  Radar uses radio waves to determine
        the range, angle, or velocity of objects.  Sibling enumerations
        provide more specific forms of radar sensing; use them when
        applicable.
    :cvar RADAR_FIRE_CONTROL: Measurement, collection or other sensing
        of radar emissions or reflections for the purpose of controlling
        a weapon via a datalink or other communications channel.
    :cvar RADAR_IMAGING: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        radar emissions or reflections for the purpose of creating
        imagery.
    :cvar RADAR_TARGETING: Use of a radar to determine the kinematics of
        a target for activities such as sensor pointing or developing
        weapon impact coordinates.  Targeting can be similar to fire
        control depending on the weapon type.
    :cvar RADAR_TRACKING: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        radar emissions or reflections for the purpose of determining
        the kinematics of one or multiple targets.
    :cvar RADAR_WEATHER: Measurement, collection or other sensing of
        radar emissions or reflections for the purpose of characterizing
        weather.
    :cvar RADIOLOGICAL: Sensing, such as a geiger counter, to determine
        the presence or characteristics of radiological materials.
    :cvar SEISMIC_VIBRATION: Detection or measurement of movement of the
        earth or objects on the earth due to natural activities or the
        movement of other objects.
    :cvar SIGINT: Signals intelligence (SIGINT) is intelligence-
        gathering by interception of signals.  Sibling enumerations
        provide more specific forms of SIGINT; use them when applicable.
    :cvar SIGINT_COMINT: Electronic signals intelligence (ELINT) is
        intelligence-gathering by interception of signals used for
        communications including telephone conversations, text messages
        and various types of online interactions.
    :cvar SIGINT_ELINT: Electronic signals intelligence (ELINT) is
        intelligence-gathering by interception of signals other than
        those used for communications.
    :cvar SIGINT_EW: Electronic warfare (EW) is any action involving the
        use of the electromagnetic spectrum (EM spectrum) or directed
        energy to control the spectrum, attack an enemy, or impede enemy
        assaults.
    :cvar SIGINT_EW_ESM: Tactical EW supporting electronic attack.
    :cvar SIGINT_FISINT: Intelligence from the interception of foreign
        electromagnetic emissions associated with the testing and
        operational deployment of foreign aerospace, surface, and
        subsurface systems.
    :cvar SONAR: Detection or measurement of sound propagation to detect
        objects on or under the surface of the water, such as other
        vessels.
    :cvar TEMPERATURE: Device that measures the temperature of its
        environment and converts the input data into electronic data to
        record, monitor, or signal temperature changes.
    """

    ACOUSTIC = "ACOUSTIC"
    AIR_SAMPLE = "AIR_SAMPLE"
    BIOLOGICAL = "BIOLOGICAL"
    CHEMICAL = "CHEMICAL"
    CONTRAIL = "CONTRAIL"
    EOIR = "EOIR"
    EOIR_FIRE_CONTROL = "EOIR_FIRE_CONTROL"
    EOIR_IMAGING = "EOIR_IMAGING"
    EOIR_TARGETING = "EOIR_TARGETING"
    EOIR_TRACKING = "EOIR_TRACKING"
    EOIR_VIDEO = "EOIR_VIDEO"
    EYESIGHT = "EYESIGHT"
    GEOINT = "GEOINT"
    HUMINT = "HUMINT"
    IMINT = "IMINT"
    MAGNETIC_ANOMALY = "MAGNETIC_ANOMALY"
    MASINT = "MASINT"
    NUCLEAR = "NUCLEAR"
    OTHER = "OTHER"
    RADAR = "RADAR"
    RADAR_FIRE_CONTROL = "RADAR_FIRE_CONTROL"
    RADAR_IMAGING = "RADAR_IMAGING"
    RADAR_TARGETING = "RADAR_TARGETING"
    RADAR_TRACKING = "RADAR_TRACKING"
    RADAR_WEATHER = "RADAR_WEATHER"
    RADIOLOGICAL = "RADIOLOGICAL"
    SEISMIC_VIBRATION = "SEISMIC_VIBRATION"
    SIGINT = "SIGINT"
    SIGINT_COMINT = "SIGINT_COMINT"
    SIGINT_ELINT = "SIGINT_ELINT"
    SIGINT_EW = "SIGINT_EW"
    SIGINT_EW_ESM = "SIGINT_EW_ESM"
    SIGINT_FISINT = "SIGINT_FISINT"
    SONAR = "SONAR"
    TEMPERATURE = "TEMPERATURE"


class SensorCategoryEnum(Enum):
    """
    An enumeration specifying the category of sensor (ex: SSN, Commercial,
    MDA).

    :cvar FOREIGN_GOV: Identifies a sensor that is controlled by a
        foreign government.
    :cvar US_GOV: Identifies a sensor that is controlled by the US
        government.
    :cvar SSN: Identifies a sensor that has a tasking agreement to
        operate as part of the U.S. Space Surveillance Network (SSN).
    :cvar COMMERCIAL: Identifies a sensor that is commercially owned.
    :cvar IC: Identifies a sensor that is controlled by the Intelligence
        Community (IC).
    :cvar MDA: Identifies a sensor that is controlled by the Missile
        Defense Agency (MDA).
    :cvar FOREIGN: Identifies a sensor that is controlled by foreign
        entities.
    :cvar FVEY: Identifies a sensor that is part of an intelligence
        sharing alliance comprising government agencies from the US,
        Great Britain, Canada, New Zealand, and Australia.
    :cvar US_GOV_RESTRICTED_CONTRACT: Identifies a sensor that is not
        owned by the U.S. Government but operated on behalf of the U.S.
        Government and under strict U.S. Government national security
        restrictions for activities.
    :cvar US_GOV_COMMERCIAL_CONTRACT: Identifies a sensor that is
        contracted for collections by the U.S. government but is under
        standard commercial restrictions for operations.
    """

    FOREIGN_GOV = "FOREIGN_GOV"
    US_GOV = "US_GOV"
    SSN = "SSN"
    COMMERCIAL = "COMMERCIAL"
    IC = "IC"
    MDA = "MDA"
    FOREIGN = "FOREIGN"
    FVEY = "FVEY"
    US_GOV_RESTRICTED_CONTRACT = "US_GOV_RESTRICTED_CONTRACT"
    US_GOV_COMMERCIAL_CONTRACT = "US_GOV_COMMERCIAL_CONTRACT"


