class SpeedLimitTypeEnum(Enum):
    """
    An enumeration indicating the most common types of speed limits defined
    by Federal Aviation Regulations. (Code of Federal Regulations: Title 14
    Aeronautics and Space).

    :cvar V1_MAXIMUM_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED: The speed beyond which
        takeoff should no longer be aborted. The maximum speed in the
        takeoff at which the pilot must take the first action (e.g.,
        apply brakes, reduce thrust, deploy speed brakes) to stop the
        airplane within the accelerate-stop distance. V1 also means the
        minimum speed in the takeoff, following a failure of the
        critical engine at VEF, at which the pilot can continue the
        takeoff and achieve the required height above the takeoff
        surface within the takeoff distance.
    :cvar V2_TAKEOFF_SAFETY_SPEED: Takeoff safety speed. The speed at
        which the aircraft may safely climb with one engine inoperative.
    :cvar V2_MIN_MINIMUM_TAKEOFF_SPEED: Minimum takeoff safety speed.
    :cvar V3_FLAP_RETRACTION_SPEED: Flap retraction speed.
    :cvar V4_CLIMB_SPEED: Steady initial climb speed. The all engines
        operating take-off climb speed used to the point where
        acceleration to flap retraction speed is initiated.
    :cvar VA_MANEUVER_SPEED: Design maneuvering speed. This is the speed
        above which it is unwise to make full application of any single
        flight control as it may generate a force greater than the
        aircraft's structural limitations.
    :cvar VAT_APPROACH_THRESHOLD_SPEED: Indicated airspeed at threshold,
        which is usually equal to the stall speed VS0 multiplied by 1.3
        or stall speed VS1g multiplied by 1.23 in the landing
        configuration at the maximum certificated landing mass, though
        some manufacturers apply different criteria. If both VS0 and
        VS1g are available, the higher resulting Vat shall be applied.
        Also called "approach speed". Also known as Vth.
    :cvar VB_GUST_SPEED: Design speed for maximum gust intensity.
    :cvar VC_CRUISE_SPEED: Design cruise, also known as the optimum
        cruise speed, is the most efficient speed in terms of distance,
        speed and fuel usage.
    :cvar VCEF_CRITICAL_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED: See V1; generally used
        in documentation of military aircraft performance. Denotes
        "critical engine failure" speed as the speed during takeoff
        where the same distance would be required to either continue the
        takeoff or abort to a stop.
    :cvar VD_DIVING_SPEED: Design diving speed, the highest speed
        planned to be achieved in testing.
    :cvar VDF_DEMONSTRATED_FLIGHT_DIVING_SPEED: Demonstrated flight
        diving speed, the highest actual speed achieved in testing.
    :cvar VEF_CRITICAL_ENGINE_FAILURE_SPEED: The speed at which the
        critical engine is assumed to fail during takeoff.
    :cvar VF_FLAP_SPEED: Designed flap speed.
    :cvar VFC_MAXIMUM_STABILITY_SPEED: Maximum speed for stability
        characteristics.
    :cvar VFE_MAXIMUM_FLAP_EXTENDED_SPEED: Maximum flap extended speed.
    :cvar VFTO_FINAL_TAKEOFF_SPEED: Final takeoff speed.
    :cvar VH_MAXIMUM_LEVEL_FLIGHT_SPEED: Maximum speed in level flight
        at maximum continuous power.
    :cvar VLE_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_EXTENDED_SPEED: Maximum landing gear
        extended speed. This is the maximum speed at which a retractable
        gear aircraft should be flown with the landing gear extended.
    :cvar VLO_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_OPERATING_SPEED: Maximum landing gear
        operating speed. This is the maximum speed at which the landing
        gear on a retractable gear aircraft should be extended or
        retracted.
    :cvar VLOF_LIFT_OFF_SPEED: Lift-off speed.
    :cvar VMC_MINIMUM_CONTROL_SPEED: Minimum control speed. The minimum
        speed at which the aircraft is still controllable with the
        critical engine inoperative. VMC is sometimes further refined
        into more discrete V-speeds e.g. VMCA,VMCG.
    :cvar VMCA_MINIMUM_CONTROL_AIR_SPEED: Minimum control speed air. The
        minimum speed that the aircraft is still controllable with the
        critical engine inoperative while the aircraft is airborne. VMCA
        is sometimes simply referred to as VMC.
    :cvar VMCG_MINIMUM_CONTROL_GROUND_SPEED: Minimum control speed
        ground. The minimum speed that the aircraft is still
        controllable with the critical engine inoperative while the
        aircraft is on the ground.
    :cvar VMCL_MINIMUM_CONTROL_LANDING_SPEED: Minimum control speed in
        the landing configuration with one engine inoperative.
    :cvar VMO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_SPEED: Maximum operating limit speed.
        Exceeding VMO may trigger an overspeed alarm.
    :cvar VMU_MINIMUM_UNSTICK_SPEED: Minimum unstick speed.
    :cvar VNE_NEVER_EXCEED_SPEED: Never exceed speed. In a helicopter,
        this is chosen to prevent retreating blade stall and prevent the
        advancing blade from going supersonic.
    :cvar VNO_MAXIMUM_CRUISING_SPEED: Maximum structural cruising speed
        or maximum speed for normal operations. Speed at which exceeding
        the limit load factor may cause permanent deformation of the
        aircraft structure.
    :cvar VO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_MANEUVER_SPEED: Maximum operating
        maneuvering speed.
    :cvar VR_ROTATION_SPEED: Rotation speed. The speed at which the
        pilot begins to apply control inputs to cause the aircraft nose
        to pitch up, after which it will leave the ground.
    :cvar VROT_ROTATION_SPEED: Used instead of VR (in discussions of the
        takeoff performance of military aircraft) to denote rotation
        speed in conjunction with the term Vref (refusal speed).
    :cvar VREF_LANDING_REFERENCE_SPEED: Landing reference speed or
        threshold crossing speed. Must be at least 1.3 VS0. Must be at
        least VMC for reciprocating-engine aircraft, or 1.05 VMC for
        commuter category aircraft. In discussions of the takeoff
        performance of military aircraft, the term Vref stands for
        refusal speed. Refusal speed is the maximum speed during takeoff
        from which the air vehicle can stop within the available
        remaining runway length for a specified altitude, weight, and
        configuration. Incorrectly, or as an abbreviation, some
        documentation refers to Vref and/or Vrot speeds as "Vr."
    :cvar VS_FLIGHT_STALL_SPEED: Stall speed or minimum steady flight
        speed for which the aircraft is still controllable.
    :cvar VS0_LANDING_STALL_SPEED: Stall speed or minimum flight speed
        in landing configuration.
    :cvar VS1_MINIMUM_FLIGHT_STALL_SPEED: Stall speed or minimum steady
        flight speed for which the aircraft is still controllable in a
        specific configuration.
    :cvar VSR_REFERENCE_STALL_SPEED: Reference stall speed.
    :cvar VSR0_REFERENCE_LANDING_STALL_SPEED: Reference stall speed in
        landing configuration.
    :cvar VSR1_REFERENCE_SPECIFIC_STALL_SPEED: Reference stall speed in
        a specific configuration.
    :cvar VSW_STALL_WARNING_SPEED: Speed at which the stall warning will
        occur.
    :cvar VTOSS_CATEGORY_A_TAKEOFF_SAFETY_SPEED: Category A rotorcraft
        takeoff safety speed.
    :cvar VX_BEST_CLIMB_ANGLE_SPEED: Speed that will allow for best
        angle of climb.
    :cvar VY_BEST_CLIMB_RATE_SPEED: Speed that will allow for the best
        rate of climb.
    """

    V1_MAXIMUM_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED = "V1_MAXIMUM_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED"
    V2_TAKEOFF_SAFETY_SPEED = "V2_TAKEOFF_SAFETY_SPEED"
    V2_MIN_MINIMUM_TAKEOFF_SPEED = "V2MIN_MINIMUM_TAKEOFF_SPEED"
    V3_FLAP_RETRACTION_SPEED = "V3_FLAP_RETRACTION_SPEED"
    V4_CLIMB_SPEED = "V4_CLIMB_SPEED"
    VA_MANEUVER_SPEED = "VA_MANEUVER_SPEED"
    VAT_APPROACH_THRESHOLD_SPEED = "VAT_APPROACH_THRESHOLD_SPEED"
    VB_GUST_SPEED = "VB_GUST_SPEED"
    VC_CRUISE_SPEED = "VC_CRUISE_SPEED"
    VCEF_CRITICAL_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED = (
        "VCEF_CRITICAL_TAKEOFF_DECISION_SPEED"
    )
    VD_DIVING_SPEED = "VD_DIVING_SPEED"
    VDF_DEMONSTRATED_FLIGHT_DIVING_SPEED = (
        "VDF_DEMONSTRATED_FLIGHT_DIVING_SPEED"
    )
    VEF_CRITICAL_ENGINE_FAILURE_SPEED = "VEF_CRITICAL_ENGINE_FAILURE_SPEED"
    VF_FLAP_SPEED = "VF_FLAP_SPEED"
    VFC_MAXIMUM_STABILITY_SPEED = "VFC_MAXIMUM_STABILITY_SPEED"
    VFE_MAXIMUM_FLAP_EXTENDED_SPEED = "VFE_MAXIMUM_FLAP_EXTENDED_SPEED"
    VFTO_FINAL_TAKEOFF_SPEED = "VFTO_FINAL_TAKEOFF_SPEED"
    VH_MAXIMUM_LEVEL_FLIGHT_SPEED = "VH_MAXIMUM_LEVEL_FLIGHT_SPEED"
    VLE_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_EXTENDED_SPEED = (
        "VLE_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_EXTENDED_SPEED"
    )
    VLO_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_OPERATING_SPEED = (
        "VLO_MAXIMUM_LANDING_GEAR_OPERATING_SPEED"
    )
    VLOF_LIFT_OFF_SPEED = "VLOF_LIFT_OFF_SPEED"
    VMC_MINIMUM_CONTROL_SPEED = "VMC_MINIMUM_CONTROL_SPEED"
    VMCA_MINIMUM_CONTROL_AIR_SPEED = "VMCA_MINIMUM_CONTROL_AIR_SPEED"
    VMCG_MINIMUM_CONTROL_GROUND_SPEED = "VMCG_MINIMUM_CONTROL_GROUND_SPEED"
    VMCL_MINIMUM_CONTROL_LANDING_SPEED = "VMCL_MINIMUM_CONTROL_LANDING_SPEED"
    VMO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_SPEED = "VMO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_SPEED"
    VMU_MINIMUM_UNSTICK_SPEED = "VMU_MINIMUM_UNSTICK_SPEED"
    VNE_NEVER_EXCEED_SPEED = "VNE_NEVER_EXCEED_SPEED"
    VNO_MAXIMUM_CRUISING_SPEED = "VNO_MAXIMUM_CRUISING_SPEED"
    VO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_MANEUVER_SPEED = "VO_MAXIMUM_OPERATING_MANEUVER_SPEED"
    VR_ROTATION_SPEED = "VR_ROTATION_SPEED"
    VROT_ROTATION_SPEED = "VROT_ROTATION_SPEED"
