class SubsystemStateEnum(Enum):
    """
    Indicates the overall status/state of the Subsystem.

    See enumeration annotations for further details.

    :cvar UNKNOWN: Indicates the subsystem is in an unknown state.
    :cvar NOT_INSTALLED: Indicates the subsystem is not installed.
    :cvar OFF: Indicates the subsystem is in an OFF state as it was not
        powered up.
    :cvar PRE_INITIALIZATION: Indicates the subsystem is performing
        their bootstrap and initial OFP load.
    :cvar INITIALIZATION: Indicates the subsystem is performing its
        initialization and mission data load.
    :cvar STANDBY: Indicates the subsystem has completed its
        initialization and is ready to transition to the operation
        state.
    :cvar OPERATE: Indicates the subsystem is allowed to perform its
        enabled capabilities.
    :cvar OPERATE_RX_ONLY: Indicates the subsystem is allowed to perform
        its enabled receive only capabilities.
    :cvar OPERATE_TX_ONLY: Indicates the subsystem is allowed to perform
        its enabled transmit only capabilities.
    :cvar MAINTENANCE: Indicates the subsystem is performing or has
        performed its maintenance procedure.
    :cvar CALIBRATION: Indicates the Subsystem state of calibration.
        This form of calibration is initiated via SubsystemStateCommand
        and interrupts other functions.  Some Subsystems support a form
        of calibration that is initiated via SubsystemBIT_Command,
        doesn't require a Subsystem state change and doesn't interrupt
        other Subsystem functions.  See
        SubsystemCalibrationConfiguration for further details regarding
        the difference between types of commanded/initiated calibration.
    :cvar INITIATED_BIT: Indicates the Subsystem state of Initiated
        Built In Test (BIT).  This form of initiated BIT is initiated
        via SubsystemStateCommand and interrupts other functions.  Some
        Subsystems support a form of initiated BIT that is initiated via
        SubsystemBIT_Command, doesn't require a Subsystem state change
        and doesn't interrupt other Subsystem functions.  See
        SubsystemBIT_Configuration for further details regarding the
        difference between types of commanded/initiated BIT.
    :cvar SHUTDOWN: Indicates the subsystem is performing or has
        performed its shutdown procedure. Once complete, no messages
        will be sent by the subsystem.
    :cvar DEGRADED: A subsystem is considered degraded when a non-
        critical anomaly is encountered restricting the subsystem from
        performing the mission in its entirety but is still able to
        perform at least one use case within the mission.  The following
        is a non-exhaustive list of examples that could cause a
        subsystem to enter a DEGRADED state; - Redundant component
        failed but subsystem is still operational. - Decline in quality
        of service and/or functionality. - Mismatch of discretes. -
        Subset of components has failed however, functionality is still
        available.
    """

    UNKNOWN = "UNKNOWN"
    NOT_INSTALLED = "NOT_INSTALLED"
    OFF = "OFF"
    PRE_INITIALIZATION = "PRE_INITIALIZATION"
    INITIALIZATION = "INITIALIZATION"
    STANDBY = "STANDBY"
    OPERATE = "OPERATE"
    OPERATE_RX_ONLY = "OPERATE_RX_ONLY"
    OPERATE_TX_ONLY = "OPERATE_TX_ONLY"
    MAINTENANCE = "MAINTENANCE"
    CALIBRATION = "CALIBRATION"
    INITIATED_BIT = "INITIATED_BIT"
    SHUTDOWN = "SHUTDOWN"
    DEGRADED = "DEGRADED"


