class CapabilityCommandTemporalConstraintsType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar temporal_criticality: Indicates temporal scheduling of the
        Command is critical in order for the Command's results to be
        useful.  This element amplifies the sibling elements by
        explicitly stating which *must* be met.  If omitted, scheduling
        the command to satisfy the sibling elements isn't critical; the
        sibling element can be used as guidance if given but the command
        should still be scheduled even if they aren't all satisfied.
    :ivar start_time_window: Indicates the start time window for the
        command, including repetition.  The beginning of the range
        represents a start-no-earlier-than time.  The end of the range
        represents a start-no-later-than time.  If omitted, the command
        should be scheduled for immediate start within other scheduling
        constraints.
    :ivar window_on_first_only: If present, indicates the sibling
        StartTimeWindow applies to only the first command of a repeating
        series. If not present, indicates the sibling StartTimeWindow
        applies to only all (first and all subsequent) commands in a
        repeating series if element is not present.  Optional for non-
        repeating commands.
    :ivar end_time_window: Indicates the end time window for the
        command, including repetition.  The beginning of the range
        represents an end-no-earlier-than time.  The end of the range
        represents an end-no-later-than time.  If omitted, end time is
        left to the discretion of the command recipient.
    """

