@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class CollectionConstraintsType:
    """
    Modeled after SensorSpecificData in the ACTDF standard.

    :ivar map_angle_constraints: True Map Angle.  The true map angle is
        defined in the Northeast Down (NED) coordinate system with the
        origin at the aircraft (aircraft local NED) as the angle between
        the scene entry line of sight and the instantaneous aircraft
        track heading vector. The aircraft track heading vector is
        obtained by rotating the north unit vector of the aircraft local
        NED coordinate system in the aircraft local NE plane through the
        aircraft track heading angle.  This angle is always positive.
    :ivar grazing_angle_constraints: The angle at the target between the
        plane of the terrain and the line of sight to the sensor.  If
        the slope of the terrain is zero, this element is equivalent to
        the sibling ElevationAngleConstraints.
    :ivar look_angle_constraints: The angle from true north to the line-
        of-sight vector from the sensor to the target tangent plane.
    :ivar elevation_angle_constraints: The angle at the target between
        the flat surface (ellipsoid surface ignoring terrain) and the
        line of sight to the sensor.  If the slope of the terrain is
        zero, this element is equivalent to the sibling
        GrazingAngleConstraints.
    :ivar slant_range_constraints: Distance from the sensor reference
        point (e.g. aperture reference point) to the ground reference
        point.
    :ivar collection_pattern: This element defines the type of pattern
        that a vehicle should use to collect over a large area.  This
        can be specified when creating Tasks to collect over OpZones,
        ZoneTargets, Entities (which have been specified as zones), etc.
    """

