@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class FuzeType:
    """
    Weapon fuze mode and setting.

    See operational handbooks and TTP manuals for allowable fuze modes and
    settings.

    :ivar fuze_trigger: Indicates information for fuze height of burst
        and fuze delay time.
    :ivar fuze_mode: Fuze modes defined here are derived from
        operational handbooks and TTP manuals.  Impact is a type of fuze
        designed to function upon impact or after delay. The time delay
        (if any) is measured from the instant of impact. The proximity
        fuze is a miniature Doppler radar set. The lag time between
        transmission and reception is precomputed and translated into
        selectable burst height values in altitude above the target. In
        a time fuze, the delay is initiated at bomb release from the
        aircraft and not at the instant of impact. The hydrostatic type
        of fuze is employed in depth bombs for underwater demolition
        work.
    :ivar fuze_position: For weapons with multiple fuzes, indicates
        which fuze the sibling elements apply to.  Optional for weapons
        with a single fuze.
    :ivar mnemonic: The name of the fuze.
    :ivar fuze_separation_arm_time: This indicates the time at which the
        fuze will arm after separating from the aircraft.  Prior to that
        time, the fuze will not detonate, even if a fuze trigger is hit.
        This prevents fragmenting the vehicle if the weapon blows back
        into the aircraft or if it is flying very low.  Once the fuze
        separation arm time elapses, the fuze is armed and the weapon is
        hot, it will detonate when the fuze trigger hits.
    """

