@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class DeCapabilityType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar capability_id: Indicates the unique ID of this Capability.
        This ID is used to invoke the Capability via Command messages,
        report its activity via Activity messages, etc.
    :ivar capability_type: Indicates the Capability's first tier type in
        the DE taxonomy. For DE, the first tier is an indication of the
        type of weapon. See enumerated type annotations for further
        details.
    :ivar sub_capability_type: Indicates a SubCapability of the DE
        Capability, the second tier in the taxonomy of DE. For DE, the
        second tier is the means of initiation of the Capability:
        manually, semi-automatically, or automatically. See enumeration
        annotations for further details.
    :ivar accepted_interface: Indicates an accepted control interface
        for the Capability. See enumeration annotations for further
        details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That
        Apply" condition.
    :ivar capability_options: Indicates the Capability's support for
        select optional elements in its accepted control interface
        messages. Support for these elements is expected to vary across
        Capability implementations but must be known in order to adapt
        and configure upstream Systems and Services which use the
        Capability.
    :ivar eye_safe: Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the
        Capability is operable when the host Subsystem is in an eye safe
        configuration.
    :ivar associated_component_id: Indicates a command and control
        relevant Subsystem Component associated with the Capability.
        Multiple Capabilities can use the same Component.
    :ivar message_output: Indicates a message that is an output of the
        Capability. See enumerated type annotations for details. List
        size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply"
        condition.
    :ivar comms_required: If present, indicates communications are
        required to use the Capability. For example, an unmanned system
        with no onboard storage would require communications to
        disseminate the outputs of the Capability.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "DE_CapabilityType"

    capability_id: CapabilityIdType = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "CapabilityID",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        }
    )
