@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ImageSubheaderRevAType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar target_identifier: See simple type documentation. This field
        contains the identification of the primary target in the format,
        BBBBBBBBBBOOOOOCC, consisting of ten characters of Basic
        Encyclopedia (BE) identifier, followed by five characters of
        facility OSUFFIX, followed by the two character Country Code as
        specified in Geopolitical Entities and Codes (GEC) (formerly
        FIPS PUB 10-4). Default is ASCII spaces for all or any sub-part
        of this field. For use in the NITF Image Subheader TGTID,
        available from a concatenation of ACTDF BE Number and ACTDF
        Country Code.
    :ivar iid2: NITF ImageSubheader Image Identifier 2, defined herein
        for either non-IPON-compliant NTIF producers or IPON-compliant
        NITF producers, mutually exclusively.
    :ivar image_security_classification: See simple type documentation.
        REQUIRED FIELD. NITF Image Subheader ISCLAS from ACTDF Primary
        Imagery Marking Guidance section Classification field. This
        field shall contain a valid value representing the
        classification level of the entire file. Valid values are T
        (=Top Secret), S (=Secret), C (=Confidential), R (=Restricted),
        U (=Unclassified).
    :ivar image_security_classification_system: See simple type
        documentation. NITF Image Subheader ISCLSY from ACTDF Primary
        Imagery Marking Guidance section Image Security Classification
        System. This field shall contain valid values indicating the
        national or multinational security system used to classify the
        file. Country Codes per FIPS PUB 10-4 shall be used to indicate
        national security systems. The designator "XN" is for classified
        data generated by a component using NATO security system marking
        guidance. This code is outside the FIPS 10-4/GEC document
        listing, and was selected to not duplicate that document's
        existing codes. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall
        imply that no security classification system applies to the
        file.  NOTE: If ISCLAS is T, S, C, or R, then ISCLSY must be
        populated with a valid code for the security classification
        system used.  NOTE: If any of the following fields are populated
        with anything other than spaces, then FileClassificationSystem
        (FSCLSY) must be populated with a valid code for the security
        classification system used: ISCODE, ISREL, ISDCTP, ISDCDT,
        ISDCXM, ISDG, ISDGDT, ISCLTX, ISCATP, ISCAUT, ISCRSN, ISSRDT,
        and ISCTLN.
    :ivar image_codewords: See simple type documentation. NITF Image
        Subheader ISCODE from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking Guidance
        section Image Codewords. This field shall contain a valid
        indicator of the security compartments associated with the file.
        Values include zero to four of the digraphs found in MIL-
        STD-2500x Table A-4 (2 CAP alphas) each separated by a single
        ECS space (0x20): The selection of a relevant set of codewords
        is application specific. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20),
        it shall imply that no codewords apply to the file.
    :ivar image_control_and_handling: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISCTLH from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Control and Handling. This field shall
        contain valid additional security control and/or handling
        instructions (caveats) associated with the file. Values include
        any one of the digraphs found in MIL-STD-2500x Table A-4 - the
        digraph in the OTHER CODEWORDS row may indicate single or
        multiple caveats and apparently may be any two ECS-A characters,
        not just CAP alphas. The selection of a relevant caveat or
        caveats is application specific. If this field is all ECS spaces
        (0x20), it shall imply that no additional control and handling
        instructions apply to the file.
    :ivar image_releasing_instructions: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISREL from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Releasable To. This field shall contain a valid
        list of country and/or multilateral entity codes to which
        countries and/or multilateral entities the file is authorized
        for release. Valid items in the list are one to 7 country codes
        as found in Geopolitical Entities and Codes (formerly FIPS PUB
        10-4) separated by a single ECS space (0x20). If this field is
        all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no file release
        instructions apply.
    :ivar image_declassification_type: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISDCTP from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Declassification Type. This field shall
        contain a valid indicator of the type of security
        declassification or downgrading instructions which apply to the
        file. Valid values are DD (=declassify on a specific date), DE
        (=declassify upon occurrence of an event), GD (=downgrade to a
        specified level on a specific date), GE (=downgrade to a
        specified level upon occurrence of an event), O (=OADR), and X
        (= exempt from automatic declassification). If this field is not
        present, it implies that no file security declassification or
        downgrading instructions apply.
    :ivar image_declassification_date: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISDCDT from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Declass Date. This field shall indicate the
        date (CCYYMMDD) on which a file is to be declassified if the
        value in File Declassification Type is DD. If this field is all
        ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that no file declassification
        date applies.
    :ivar image_declassification_exemption: See simple type
        documentation. NITF Image Subheader ISDCXM from ACTDF Primary
        Imagery Marking Guidance section Declass Exception. This field
        shall indicate the reason the file is exempt from automatic
        declassification if the value in File Declassification Type is
        X. Valid values are X1 to X8 and X251 to X259. X1 to X8
        correspond to the declassification exemptions found in DOD
        5200.1-R, paragraphs 4-202b(1) to (8) for material exempt from
        the 10-year rule. X251 to X259 correspond to the
        declassification exemptions found in DOD 5200.1-R, paragraphs
        4-301a(1) to (9) for permanently valuable material exempt from
        the 25-year declassification system. If this field is all ESC
        spaces (0x20), it shall imply that a file declassification
        exemption does not apply.
    :ivar image_downgrade: See simple type documentation. NITF Image
        Subheader ISDG from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking Guidance
        section Image Downgrade. This field shall indicate the
        classification level to which a file is to be downgraded if the
        values in File Declassification Type are GD or GE. Valid values
        are S (=Secret), C (=Confidential), R (=Restricted). If this
        field contains an ECS space (0x20), it shall imply that file
        security downgrading does not apply.
    :ivar image_downgrade_date: See simple type documentation. NITF
        Image Subheader ISDGDT from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Downgrade Date. This field shall indicate
        the date (CCYYMMDD) on which a file is to be downgraded if the
        value in File Declassification Type is GD. If this field is all
        ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that a file security
        downgrading date does not apply.
    :ivar image_classification_text: See simple type documentation. NITF
        Image Subheader ISCLTX from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section File Classification Text. This field shall be
        used to provide additional information about file classification
        to include identification of a declassification or downgrading
        event if the values in File Declassification Type are DE or GE.
        It may also be used to identify multiple classification sources
        and/or any other special handling rules. Values are user defined
        free text. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall
        imply that additional information about file classification does
        not apply.Note that chars in the range 0xA0 to 0xFF should be
        avoided.
    :ivar image_classification_authority_type: See simple type
        documentation. NITF Image Subheader ISCATP from ACTDF Primary
        Imagery Marking Guidance section Image Classification Authority
        Type. This field indicates the type of authority used to
        classify the file. Valid values are O (= original classification
        authority), D (= derivative from a single source), and M (=
        derivative from multiple sources). If this field contains an ECS
        space (0x20), it implies that file classification authority type
        does not apply.
    :ivar image_classification_authority: Image Classification Authority
        aka Image Classified By. See simple type documentation. NITF
        Image Subheader ISCAUT from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Classified By. This field shall identify the
        classification authority for the file dependent upon the value
        in File Classification Authority Type. Values are user defined
        free text which should contain the following information:
        original classification authority name and position or personal
        identifier if the value in File Classification Authority Type is
        O; title of the document or security classification guide used
        to classify the file if the value in File Classification
        Authority Type is D; and Derive-Multiple if the file
        classification was derived from multiple sources and the value
        of the ISCATP field is M. In the latter case, the file
        originator will maintain a record of the sources used in
        accordance with existing security directives. One of the
        multiple sources may also be identified in File Classification
        Text if desired. If this field is all ECS spaces (0x20), it
        shall imply that no file classification authority applies.
    :ivar image_classification_reason: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISCRSN from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Classification Reason. This field
        contains values indicating the reason for classifying the file.
        Valid values are A to G. These correspond to the reasons for
        original classification per E.O. 12958, Section 1.5.(a) to (g).
        If this field contains an ASCII space (0x20), it means that no
        file classification reason applies.
    :ivar image_security_source_date: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISSRDT from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Security Source Date in form CCYYMMDD.
        This field shall indicate the date of the source used to derive
        the classification of the file. In the case of multiple sources,
        the date of the most recent source shall be used. If this field
        is all ECS spaces (0x20), it shall imply that a file security
        source date does not apply.
    :ivar image_security_control_number: See simple type documentation.
        NITF Image Subheader ISCTLN from ACTDF Primary Imagery Marking
        Guidance section Image Security Control Number. This field shall
        contain a valid security control number associated with the
        file. The format of the security control number shall be in
        accordance with the regulations governing the appropriate
        security channel or channels. If this field is all ECS spaces
        (0x20), it shall imply that no file security control number
        applies.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "ImageSubheaderRevA_Type"

