class RtnKinematicsType:
    """
    Indicates kinematic vectors in the Radial-Transverse-Normal (RTN)
    reference frame, also known as the Radial, In-Track, Cross-Track (RIC)
    reference frame.

    The Radial basis vector is aligned with the position vector. The Normal
    basis vector is aligned with the angular momentum direction (which is
    the orbit normal direction). The Transverse basis vector is in the
    direction of N x R to complete the right-handed triad.

    :ivar epoch: Indicates the time when the kinematic data is valid.
    :ivar position: Indicates a position vector in the RTN reference
        frame.
    :ivar velocity: Indicates a velocity vector in the RTN reference
        frame.
    :ivar acceleration: Indicates an acceleration vector in the RTN
        reference frame.
    :ivar attitude: Indicates the attitude in the RTN reference frame.
    :ivar covariance: The covariance matrix along with its associated
        category that defines the elements represented in the covariance
        matrix in the RTN reference frame.  See the individual category
        enumerations for detailed explanations.
    """

