@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class DlzDataType:
    """
    This type contains the data necessary for a DLZ.

    :ivar range_turn_and_close: Launch slant range at which the weapon
        will intercept the target and arm its fuze, assuming no platform
        guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current steering
        2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed)
        3.Target turn-and-close maneuver RangeTurnandClose is not
        applicable to ballistic trajectory targets.
    :ivar range_minimum: Launch slant range at which the weapon will
        intercept the target and arm its fuze, assuming no platform
        guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current steering
        2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed)
        3.No target maneuvers Note: ballistic trajectory velocity
        changes are not considered maneuvers.
    :ivar range_turn_and_run: Launch range at which the weapon will
        intercept the target with high energy, assuming no platform
        guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current steering
        2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed)
        3.Target turn-and-run maneuver RangeTurnAndRun is not applicable
        to ballistic trajectory targets.
    :ivar range_probability_of_intercept: Launch range at which the
        weapon will intercept the target with high energy, assuming no
        platform guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current
        steering 2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g.,
        altitude/airspeed) 3.No target maneuvers Note: ballistic
        trajectory velocity changes are not considered maneuvers.
    :ivar range_max_guidance: Launch range at which the weapon will
        intercept the target with nominal energy, assuming no platform
        guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current steering
        2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed)
        3.No target maneuvers, Note: ballistic trajectory velocity
        changes are not considered maneuvers.
    :ivar range_optimal: Launch range at which the weapon will intercept
        the target with high energy, assuming no platform guidance or
        weapon guidance errors for: 1.Optimal steering 2.Current shooter
        kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed) 3.No target
        maneuvers, Note: ballistic trajectory velocity changes are not
        considered maneuvers.
    :ivar range_max_aero: Launch range at which the weapon will
        intercept the target with nominal energy, assuming no platform
        guidance or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Optimal steering
        2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed)
        3.No target maneuvers, Note: ballistic trajectory velocity
        changes are not considered maneuvers.
    :ivar target_closure_rate: The target closure rate as a velocity in
        meters-per-second.
    :ivar target_range: The slant range to the target.
    :ivar weapon_to_target_seeker_activation_range: The range from the
        weapon to the target at weapon seeker activation, assuming no
        platform guidance errors or weapon guidance errors. This data is
        only applicable to weapons with an end-game seeker.
    :ivar weapon_to_target_autonomous_range: The range from the weapon
        to the target when the weapon is autonomous (does not require
        data link support). This data is only applicable to weapons with
        a data link.
    :ivar weapon_to_target_mprfrange: The range from the weapon to the
        target when the weapon activates its Medium Pulse Repetition
        Frequency mode, assuming no platform guidance errors or weapon
        guidance errors. This data is only applicable to weapons with
        active seekers which implement a MPRF mode.
    :ivar a_pole: The range from the shooter to the target when the
        weapon activates its seeker, assuming no platform or weapon
        guidance errors for:                1.Current steering 2.Current
        shooter kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed) 3.No
        target maneuvers This data is only applicable to weapons with an
        end-game seeker.
    :ivar f_pole: The range from the shooter to the target when the
        weapon intercepts/impacts the target, assuming no platform or
        weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current steering 2.Current shooter
        kinematic conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed), and 3.No target
        maneuvers
    :ivar m_pole: The range from the shooter to the target when the
        weapon activates its Medium Pulse Repetition Frequency mode,
        assuming no platform or weapon guidance errors for: 1.Current
        steering 2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g.,
        altitude/airspeed) 3.No target maneuvers This data is only
        applicable to weapons with active seekers which implement a MPRF
        mode.
    :ivar allowable_steering_error: The maximum amount of steering error
        which will still result in a successful weapon intercept/impact
        with nominal energy.
    :ivar steering_unit_vector: Steering unit vector and its defined
        coordinate frame.
    :ivar loft_angle: Required pitch angle to get to the maximum aero
        range for the missile.
    :ivar digital_manuvering_cue_angle: The magnitude of the maximum
        angle the target can turn away from the platform which results
        in weapon intercept of the target with nominal energy, assuming
        an immediate employment command.  This field is valid only if
        RangeMaxGuidance &gt;= TargetRange &gt;= RangeTurnandRun.  This
        field is never greater than the magnitude of the target aspect
        angle. For air platforms, this turn is in the horizontal plane
        defined by the north and east axes.
    :ivar time_of_intercept: The time of weapon intercept/impact of the
        target, assuming no platform guidance or weapon errors, for:
        1.Current steering 2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g.,
        altitude/airspeed) 3.No post-launch target maneuvers
    :ivar time_to_release: The seconds time to activate for the proposed
        launch store type.
    :ivar time_of_activation: The time of weapon seeker activation,
        assuming no platform guidance or weapon errors, for: 1.Current
        steering 2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g.,
        altitude/airspeed) 3.No post-launch target maneuvers
    :ivar time_of_mprf: The time of weapon seeker MPRF (for weapons with
        MPRF mode), assuming no platform guidance or weapon errors, for:
        1.Current steering 2.Current shooter kinematic conditions (e.g.,
        altitude/airspeed) 3.No post-launch target maneuvers
    :ivar time_of_autonomous: The time of weapon being autonomous (not
        using data link), assuming no platform guidance or weapon
        errors, for: 1.Current steering 2.Current shooter kinematic
        conditions (e.g., altitude/airspeed) 3.No post-launch target
        maneuvers
    """

