@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class DmpiDesignationRequestMdt(RequestBaseType):
    """
    See annotations in child elements and associated global element
    (message) for further details.

    :ivar task_id: Indicates the ID of the strike Task from which the
        DMPI designation should be derived.
    :ivar product_metadata_id: Indicates the IDs of the data product
        from which this DMPI designation should be derived.  It should
        be considered required in cases where the DMPI designation
        requestor expects specific data products to be used to create
        the DMPI designation, such as dynamic targeting scenarios with
        freshly collected sensor products.  It is optional to support
        use cases where products aren't used to create the DMPI
        designation and/or the selection of products is left to the
        designator to select.
    :ivar recommended_weapons: Indicates a recommendation on the type
        and quantity of weapons to use when targeting and creating
        DMPIs.
    :ivar available_weapons: Indicates a constraint on the type and
        quantity of weapons available (or to be used) when targeting and
        creating DMPIs.  It is optional for cases when the system/node
        creating DMPIs has direct awareness of the plans and weapon
        type/quantity of the strike Systems and/or the requestor has
        deferred the selection.  When specified, this element is
        considered a targeting constraint to be used regardless of other
        weapon type/quantity information that may be available.
    :ivar respond_by: Indicates the time by which DMPIs must be provided
        in order for the requestor to meet their needs.
    :ivar proposed_dmpi_coordinates: The proposed coordinate for a DMPI.
        This coordinate might not be the exact point for the DMPI, but
        is used to give an estimate for the DMPI coordinate to be
        located at. This message may be used by a non-precise or display
        service to request mensurated points from a target mensuration
        service.  This information can be used to support the kill
        chain's "Find and Destroy" use case.
    :ivar reference_pixel_coordinate: The pixel coordinate for a DMPI in
        a given reference image file, given by File, ProductID or
        ForeignKey. If all of the optional fields are not there then the
        ProductMetadataID field in DMPI_DesignationRequest could be
        used. Aids in creating a DMPI based on a georegistered image.
        This information can be used to support the kill chain's "Find
        and Destroy" use case.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "DMPI_DesignationRequestMDT"

    task_id: TaskIdType = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "TaskID",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        }
    )
