@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class EntitySourceSpecificDataType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar fusion_eligibility: Indicates the eligibility of this Entity
        for automated fusion operations by the Entity's source
        System/Service and/or fusion tier.  FULL indicates that this
        Entity, and therefore its contributor Entity or Entities, is
        fully eligible for future automated fusion operations.
        SELECTIVE_EXCLUSION indicates that the Entity is eligible for
        future automated fusion operations excluding merging with the
        Entity or Entities given in the sibling CorrelatedEntity
        element.  SELECTIVE_INCLUSION indicates that the Entity is
        eligible for future automated fusion operations but only with
        the Entity or Entities given in the sibling CorrelatedEntity
        element.  NONE indicates that this Entity is not eligible for
        future automated fusion operations regardless of the associated
        Entity.  This element does not restrict operator initiated
        fusion operations via the EntityManagementRequest.
    :ivar correlated_entity_id: Indicates the unique ID of an Entity
        which is eligible for or excluded from future automated fusion
        operations with the Entity represented by this Entity message.
        This element is required when the sibling FusionEligibility
        element indicates SELECTIVE_EXCLUSION or SELECTIVE_INCLUSION and
        should be omitted otherwise.
    :ivar drop_restriction: Indicates the drop restriction on an Entity.
        These restrictions can be applied by operator action or by other
        services due to dependencies on other messages.
    :ivar ambiguous_entity_id: Indicates the unique ID of an Entity that
        for at least a singular point in time was kinematically
        uncertain with this Entity.  An example of this is when two
        vehicles come to a common intersection, stop, and then depart
        together.  Tracking algorithms have to make a decision on which
        track goes with which target and are not guaranteed to make the
        correct decision unless there are outside sources (FBCB2, High
        Range Resolution Profiles, etc.) that allow the tracker to
        either confirm the decision, or determine that a swap is
        necessary at a later time.  At the time of the intersection, the
        uncertainties of the tracks make them kinematically ambiguous so
        that information should be carried on with the fused Entity.  If
        the tracker makes the correct decision, than the other Entity
        will not be a ContributorID, since it will have never
        contributed to the overall fused picture.  Likewise, the
        Identity of the fused Entity will not be modified since the
        other Entity never made a contribution.  If the tracker makes an
        incorrect decision than the other Entity will be a ContributorID
        and will possibly contribute to the Identity of the Fused
        Entity.  Regardless of the decision, the Ambiguous ID must be
        updated to reflect the ambiguous state that occurred.
    :ivar track_quality: This element is the track quality as defined by
        MIL-STD-6016. This element represents the positional accuracy of
        the Entity, when the Entity came from a Link-16 source. It is
        the area, in square data miles, within which it is assessed that
        there is a 95% probability that the track/point lies.
    :ivar priority: Indicates the source determined priority of the
        Entity.  For example an Entity from a Capability might have an
        MDF determined priority based on the Identity and/or Signal
        characteristics of the Entity.
    :ivar passive_active_indicator: Indicates the type of sensor as
        either passive or active.
    """

    fusion_eligibility: None | EntityFusionEligibilityEnum = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "FusionEligibility",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    correlated_entity_id: list[CorrelatedEntityIdType] = field(
        default_factory=list,
        metadata={
            "name": "CorrelatedEntityID",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    drop_restriction: list[DropRestrictionType] = field(
        default_factory=list,
        metadata={
            "name": "DropRestriction",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    ambiguous_entity_id: list[EntityIdType] = field(
        default_factory=list,
        metadata={
            "name": "AmbiguousEntityID",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    track_quality: None | int = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "TrackQuality",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
            "max_inclusive": 15,
        },
    )
    priority: None | ComparableRankingType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "Priority",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    passive_active_indicator: None | PassiveActiveEnum = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "PassiveActiveIndicator",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )


