@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class RfTransmissionType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar rf_thread_instance_index: This grouping of
        RF_ThreadInstanceIndexs must be of equivalent
        ResourceAccessPriority. This set of RF_ThreadInstances cannot
        represent multiple resource allocations. ResourceAllocator
        generates the index in a an incrementing fashion 1, 2, 3... at
        resource allocation time, assuring that identifiers are unique
        across resource allocations. RF_ThreadInstanceIndices may be re-
        used after an allocation has been de-allocated.
    :ivar antenna_resource: A set of antenna resource that will be used
        for RF transmit.
    :ivar resource_access_priority: Resource Access Priority associated
        with this CIR. This is a positive ordinal integer value used to
        define arbitration priority for accesses to Shared Antenna
        Resources. This element follows the priority weighting approach
        where higher values are higher priority and lower values are
        lower priority.
    :ivar frequency: Indicates finer granularity of frequency chunks
        that this CIR Index is associated with.
    :ivar polarization: Polarization of the transmission.
    :ivar maximum_transmit_erp: Required if RF_Mode is Transmit. Maximum
        ERP of all RFTI in this CIR in dBW.
    :ivar blanking_limit: Transmit function report of acceptable amount
        of blanking. Subsystems that blank are expected not to exceed
        the TxPercentBlankLimit allocated to their subsystem.
    :ivar minimum_receive_sensitivity: It is the minimum receive
        sensitivity in the RFTI set. Receive sensitivity is the maximum
        tolerable receive input at the antenna in dBW.
    :ivar percent_interruptable: Percentage of the allocated percent
        access in which the corresponding RF Thread Instance Index can
        be interrupted.
    """

