@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class CommSupportCancelCommand(CommSupportCancelCommandMt):
    """
    This message is a request to cancel CommSupport which has been
    allocated and planned.

    A planning input such as Effect, CommSupport, Task and DMPI can't
    easily be canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions
    between their various users and publishers, inevitability of the
    associated activity, etc. Additionally, the operator or service
    initiating the cancellation might be different than the one that
    manages RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing
    additional race conditions. In order to avoid race conditions, receive
    positive feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled
    messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an
    explicit CommSupportCancelCommand is necessary. A
    CommSupportCancelCommand shall result in the CommSupport being canceled
    unless execution was already inevitable. If the CommSupport was
    inevitable and started executing but can be stopped (such as a long
    collection CommSupport) it shall cancel as soon as possible.
    CommSupportCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets to
    remove the associated CommSupport, thereby removing the CommSupport
    from the next planning cycle. Services other than those that manage
    RequirementSets and execute activities aren't required to handle
    CommSupportCancelCommand. CommSupportCancelCommand doesn't necessarily
    trigger a replan (there isn't a corresponding planning trigger),
    therefore a System could continue to navigate routes related to the
    canceled CommSupport, even though the CommSupport won't occur. A
    subsequent replan could exclude the CommSupport. Status or feedback for
    this message is given through CommSupportCancelCommandStatus but the
    resulting status of the CommSupport is given through CommSupportStatus.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class CommSupportCancelCommandStatus(CommSupportCancelCommandStatusMt):
    """
    This message is sent in response to CommSupportCancelCommand and
    indicates if the CommSupport was canceled and if not why it was not
    canceled.

    The resulting status of the CommSupport is reported in
    CommSupportStatus. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


