@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ConfigurationParameterType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar parameter_id: Identifier that uniquely refers to configuration
        parameters.
    :ivar name: Name of the configuration parameter.
    :ivar value: Current value of the configuration parameter.
    :ivar default_value: Default value of the configuration parameter.
    :ivar user_modifiable: This element can indicate whether a
        configuration parameter's value is allowed to be directly
        modified by the operator.
    :ivar type_value: Defines the atomic type that "value" should be
        interpreted as.  Useful for distinguishing between floating
        point numbers and integers.
    :ivar units: This value should be populated for any configuration
        parameter that has units.
    :ivar type_specific_restrictions: Optional list of valid options for
        this parameters.  This can either be an enum (list of string
        values) or a range for numbers.
    :ivar object_class: Defines the class of object for which these
        parameters support individual settings on specific instances.
        When specifying the override, both the ID and value of the
        specific object instance are specified. If an object class is
        not specified, specific object class settings are not supported.
    :ivar mission_environment: If present, indicates this may be used as
        in input to MissionEnvironmentOverride.
    """

