@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OperatorNotificationMdt:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and associated global element
    (message) for further details.

    :ivar operator_notification_id: Unique ID of this operator
        notification.
    :ivar operator_notification_template: Indicates the notification
        template used for populating the content of the notification.
    :ivar operator_notification_template_parameters: List of parameters
        used as substitution arguments when applying notification
        templates. If a notification template syntax defined a
        substitution token (e.g. $#) in the Title, the template
        parameters would be used to replace those tokens. For example,
        given a template Title of "System $1 violated zone $2" an
        OperatorNotification that applies that template would replace
        the $1 token with the first template parameter and the $2 with
        the second template parameter.
    :ivar title: Brief description of an operator notification. This
        human readable field will be provided to the operator as a
        summary of the notification.
    :ivar details: Detailed human readable message for display to an
        operator.  This is not to be interpreted by a machine. This
        information may be provided to an operator when they seek a more
        detailed description of a notification than what the title
        provides.
    :ivar category: Categorizes this notification for purposes of
        organization and filtering.  It is expected that the service
        function providing the notification can be represented by this
        category.  For instance, if a mission planning service is
        reporting a notification regarding a task, it should report
        PLANNING as the category, not TASKING.
    :ivar severity: Indicates the overall severity of this notification.
        Informational notifications are meant to provide informational
        context of events within the system.  Indicates the existence of
        a hazardous condition requiring immediate action to prevent loss
        of life, equipment damage, or abortion of the mission. Critical
        notifications indicate the need for immediate operator
        attention.
    :ivar location: Indicates the geolocation of the notification.
    :ivar source: Source identifiers of the notification.
    :ivar actions: Actions the originator of the notification will
        execute or may execute based on operator action commands.
    :ivar count: Occurrence count of this notification.
    :ivar occurrence_timestamp: Timestamp of when the notification event
        occurred. If the event has been repeated, this will contain the
        time of the most recent occurrence.
    :ivar priority: Optional priority of the notification. This may be
        used for ordering alerts on the HMI. Higher priority values take
        precedence over lower ones. A common range is [0,100] with
        priority 100 notification being the highest priority available.
        This element follows the priority weighting approach where
        higher values are higher priority and lower values are lower
        priority.
    :ivar aural_alert: Audible definition assigned to the notification.
    :ivar destinations: Destinations for this notification.
        Destinations include operators, users, roles and
        stations/consoles responsible for displaying or processing the
        alert.  If this element is absent, the notification should be
        considered by all relevant destinations.
    :ivar associated_message: Indicates a message that is associated
        with or the cause of the operator notification.  This element
        should be omitted if an input message was not the cause of the
        notification.
    """

