@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class TaskCancelCommand(TaskCancelCommandMt):
    """
    This message is a request to cancel a Task which has been allocated and
    planned.

    A planning input such as Effect, Action, Task and DMPI can't easily be
    canceled or removed from the System due to race conditions between
    their various users and publishers, inevitability of the associated
    activity, etc. Additionally, the operator or service initiating the
    cancellation might be different than the one that manages
    RequirementSets and/or issues *PlanCommand, introducing additional race
    conditions. In order to avoid race conditions, receive positive
    feedback on the success of the cancellation and allow canceled
    messages/objects to remain in the system for historical purposes, an
    explicit TaskCancelCommand is necessary. A TaskCancelCommand shall
    result in the Task being canceled unless execution was already
    inevitable. If the Task was inevitable and started executing but can be
    stopped (such as a long collection Task) it shall cancel as soon as
    possible. TaskCancelCommand shall result in managers of RequirementSets
    to remove the associated Task, thereby removing the Task from the next
    planning cycle. Services other than those that manage RequirementSets
    and execute activities aren't required to handle TaskCancelCommand.
    TaskCancelCommand doesn't necessarily trigger a replan (there isn't a
    corresponding planning trigger), therefore a System could continue to
    navigate routes related to the canceled Task, even though the Task
    won't occur. A subsequent replan could exclude the Task. Status or
    feedback for this message is given through TaskCancelCommandStatus but
    the resulting status of the Task is given through TaskStatus.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


