@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OpaqueSettingsCommand(OpaqueSettingsCommandMt):
    """
    This message is used to change the "settings" associated with all of
    the Opaque Capabilities of a Subsystem.

    This message represents the Opaque category of UCI Capability. Opaque
    messages advertise the minimum set of parameters necessary for
    disclosing general status and limit capacities to updating subsystem
    settings by updating Mission Data Files (MDFs). Users of the Opaque
    Class of messages should only use the minimum set of fields necessary
    to satisfy subsystem and platform interactions. The UCI Implementation
    is limited at this time to the OpaqueCapability and
    OpaqueSettingsCommand message pairs. SettingsCommands generally affect
    the subsequent operation of all applicable Capabilities of the
    Subsystem; they are considered presettings, independent of
    [Capability]Command. Opaque capabilities cannot be considered when
    using performing task allocation or route planning using the
    MissionPlanCommand message. Opaque capabilities should only be used
    when the type of payload cannot be published. Opaque capabilities
    should not be represented at different classification levels using the
    same CapabilityID. If the OpaqueCapability exists at the low level, and
    the same capability need to be represented at a higher level then the
    higher level would need its own CapabilityID and capability messages.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


