class CommCapabilityType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar action: Indicates whether this is a new link to be created, or
        an existing one that needs to be modified or deleted.
    :ivar capability: Combinations of Comm Capability and Subcapability.
    :ivar subsystem_id: The Subsystem ID. If specified this indicates
        that the capability may be present on multiple subsystems and
        these settings must be applied to a specific communication
        subsystem.
    :ivar ranking: Indicates the command's rank relative to other
        commands and rank-related overrides and tailoring.
    :ivar classification: This element provides the classification label
        that the Subsystem should place on messages and other data
        resulting from the Command.
    :ivar connection_request: Indicates the desired state of the primary
        network connection for the link being commanded.
    :ivar activate_profile_id: The Profile to which this link should be
        associated to.
    :ivar network_link_id: Indicates a unique identifier for the
        configuration of an individual network connection.  Provides for
        the correlation of network link to a new activity or to an
        existing activity that will be updated.
    :ivar common_settings: Allows the Communication Planner to deviate
        from the MDF. These configurations will be applied on top of the
        MDF therefore deviating from it.
    :ivar crypto_key: Allows the Communication Planner to apply the key
        at a specified slot. Such as selecting the appropriate VINSON
        Key.
    :ivar crypto_zeroize: Allows the Communication Planner to Zeroize
        crypto slots.
    :ivar crypto_rollover: Allows the Communication Planner to perform a
        crypto rollover to slots.
    :ivar link_port_assignments: Identifies the ports to assign to the
        connection to form the link.
    :ivar verbose_status: Provides means to control the generation of
        verbose Activity messages that provide full field reporting.
    :ivar waveform_specific_settings: Allows the Communication Planner
        to deviate from the MDF in a waveform specific manner applying
        configurations which are not common.
    :ivar link_connection_request: Indicates a command to change the
        connection status of the individual data links managed by the
        waveform. Generally, a link's connection status must be
        CONNECTED for the waveform to transmit payload data over the
        communication medium or for the waveform to receive
        transmissions from the communication medium.  Note that this
        parameter is not available until after a CommActivity is created
        and may not be available until the waveform has joined the
        network.
    """

