    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar sub_capability_type: Indicates a variant of the Capability
        (such as Link 16's CMN, DNM, etc.); the second tier in the
        taxonomy of Communications.
    :ivar connection_status: Indicates whether the waveform has joined
        the network.  The connection status reflects information about
        the waveform capability with respect to its network connectivity
        (typically at the physical and medium access control--MAC--
        layers).
    :ivar common_settings_status: Indicates general waveform
        configuration settings that apply to all waveforms.  Note that
        these settings do not apply to individual data-link connections
        provided by the waveform or to the logical link control layer
        (LLC) and above, but do apply to the physical and medium access
        control layers that are just to maintain the waveforms
        connection to the network.
    :ivar current_profile_id: The ID of the Profile to which this
        activity is currently executing with.
    :ivar user_link_status: Encapsulates the user link information that
        indicates the state and configuration of the individual user
        links, which the waveform uses to transport the payload data
        over the communication medium.
    :ivar link_port_map: Provides a reflection of what port assignments
        (IO and RF) are associated with this link. It is possible to
        have more than one to reflect multiple simultaneous paths.
    :ivar link_statistics: For the periodicity of this message this is a
        report of the statistics provided by this capability and its
        links.
    :ivar waveform_specific_settings_status: Indicates waveform state
        information regarding the waveform's network access.  (Typically
        below Medium Access Control--MAC---and physical layers.
    :ivar terminal_unique_key: Serving a similar as a MAC address in
        TCP/IP, the TerminalUnique ID provides the waveform's unique
        identifier on the network (where needed).  This value would
        typically be loaded from an MDF, where necessary.
    :ivar verbose_status: Provides current settings for the control of
        the generation of verbose Activity messages that provide full
        field reporting.
    :ivar predicted_collections: Supports interaction with a capability
        assessment function. This allows a subsystem or a model of a
        subsystem to estimate future performance.
    """

