@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OpaqueCapability(OpaqueCapabilityMt):
    """
    This message represents the Opaque category of UCI Capability.

    Opaque messages advertise the minimum set of parameters necessary for
    disclosing general status and limit capacities to updating subsystem
    settings by updating Mission Data Files (MDFs). Users of the Opaque
    Class of messages should only use the minimum set of fields necessary
    to satisfy subsystem and platform interactions. The UCI Implementation
    is limited at this time to the OpaqueCapability and
    OpaqueSettingsCommand message pairs. Opaque capabilities cannot be
    considered when using performing task allocation or route planning
    using the MissionPlanCommand message. Opaque capabilities should only
    be used when the type of payload cannot be published. Opaque
    capabilities should not be represented at different classification
    levels using the same CapabilityID. If the OpaqueCapability exists at
    the low level, and the same capability need to be represented at a
    higher level then the higher level would need its own CapabilityID and
    capability messages. This message "advertises" the mostly static
    characteristics of a mission-ready Opaque Capability (of a Subsystem of
    System) so that it can be "discovered" and used. "Discovery" can be a
    misnomer depending on your perspective. UCI Capability messages aren't
    meant to enable dynamic discovery of design details of
    never-before-seen Capabilities. They don't eliminate the need for
    future software updates or configuration files with performance
    characteristics indexed by Subsystem model number. UCI Capability
    messages are meant to support discovery of what changes for a
    Capability from mission to mission or even within the course of a
    mission, especially as it relates to command and control. In UCI
    terminology, a Capability is something a System can do that is useful
    in Missions performed by a heterogeneous family of Systems and
    Services. A [Capability]Capability message describes what a Subsystem
    is capable of doing if invoked. A [Capability]Activity message
    describes what a Capability is doing. Capabilities are aligned with end
    effects of Mission operations such as imagery collection, active target
    search, passive threat detection, electronic attack and others.
    Functions which support these end effects including turret control,
    carriage control and door control aren't considered UCI Capabilities
    but might be addressed by other UCI messages. Capabilities are the
    standardized taxonomy of high level Mission end-effects functions a
    System can perform. Further, the Capability taxonomy establishes the
    "level" at which the Mission Subsystems of a System: 1) can be
    controlled, 2) can be functionally re-integrated into new Systems
    without their application software changing, 3) are modeled by
    allocation and planning services including Task Allocation, Route
    Planning, Mission Monitoring/Contingency and Task Generation services,
    4) are modeled by Capability management services including Capability
    Manager and Capability Controllers and 5) report their configuration,
    availability and status. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


