@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class LarMdt:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and associated global element
    (message) for further details.

    :ivar lar_id: This is an ID to uniquely identify the Launch
        Acceptability Region (LAR).
    :ivar request_id: This element is required when the message is
        generated in response to a LAR_Request with
        ResultsInNativeMessage=TRUE; otherwise it is omitted.
    :ivar capability_id: Indicates the weapon Capability instance that
        this LAR is associated with.  Multiple instances of this element
        should only be given when each weapon Capability is of the same
        homogeneous weapon type and multiple weapon instances are being
        employed on a single DMPI.
    :ivar lar_type: Indicates the type of region that is being
        specified.  See enumeration annotations for further details.
    :ivar basis: This element describes the basis of the dataset used
        and/or being used for the LAR.  A LAR based on a static dataset
        (mission planned route, DMPIs, winds, etc.) or a snapshot in
        time (data at the time of a LAR_Request) is calculated once and
        results in a static LAR.  A LAR calculated periodically or upon
        changing conditions in a dynamic dataset (current vehicle
        position, measured wind, etc.) results in a dynamic LAR.
    :ivar generated_by_weapon: This element indicates if the LAR was
        generated using payload algorithms. An example where this would
        be used is when using PGMs on an aircraft that generates in the
        LAR during flight and uses different algorithms than the actual
        Capability uses to generate its LAR. There are cases where the
        difference between the algorithms can prevent release of the
        weapon.
    :ivar region: Indicates the actual geo-spatial launch acceptability
        region (LAR); a region in space where the weapon can be launched
        and satisfy the given constraints.  LARs are generally
        calculated for a specific altitude (or narrow altitude band) and
        release conditions; they are generally not a three dimensional
        volume.
    :ivar lar_details: Indicates additional details describing the LAR.
        If the LAR is the result of a LAR_Request, these details are an
        echo of it.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "LAR_MDT"

