@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class PlanningByCaseTriggerType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar capability_added: This trigger refers to a new Capability or
        SubCapability which becomes available or a previously failed
        Capability which has been restored.
    :ivar capability_failure: This trigger refers to a failure of a
        Capability and/or SubCapability needed to perform a Requirement.
    :ivar comms_lost: This trigger refers to lost comms.
    :ivar dmpi_over_designation: This trigger refers to a situation
        where the designated DMPIs exceed those initially reserved for
        the Task, if this creates a shortage for other assigned Tasks.
    :ivar dmpi_under_designation: This trigger refers to a situation
        where the designated DMPIs are less than those initially
        reserved for the task, and if weapons not designated can be used
        to perform previous unallocated tasks.
    :ivar endurance_low: This trigger refers to a low remaining
        endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power. This
        trigger can further be specialized by the definition of the
        Endurance thresholds to define the trigger.
    :ivar off_route: This trigger refers to a vehicle that has deviated
        from the planned route to such a degree that a replan is
        required.
    :ivar proximity_conflict: This trigger refers to the proximity of
        two items (Systems, Entities or other items) that exceeded a
        minimum geospatial separation limit as specified in OpRouting
        messages.
    :ivar release_point_outside_lar: This trigger refers to the location
        of a DMPI, updated LAR calculations or other changes that have
        resulted in the planned release point for a weapon falling
        outside the weapon LAR.
    :ivar route_conflict: This trigger refers to a route that exceeded a
        minimum geospatial separation limit with another item or items.
        The separation is between a planned/navigated route and other
        routes or conflicting items as specified in OpRouting messages.
    :ivar route_vulnerability: This trigger refers to vulnerability due
        to exposure along the route with and without suppression.
    :ivar system_state_change: This trigger refers to a system state
        transition, as indicated by the SystemStatus message.
    :ivar requirement_added: This trigger indicates a new Requirement.
    :ivar requirement_dependency_failed: This trigger indicates a
        Requirement that cannot be planned/performed because a
        Requirement it is dependent on cannot be planned/performed.
    :ivar requirement_dropped: This trigger refers to a Requirement
        execution state transition to DROPPED, as indicated by execution
        status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus,
        etc.).
    :ivar requirement_failed: This trigger refers to a Requirement
        execution state transition to FAILED, as indicated by execution
        status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus,
        etc.).
    :ivar requirement_change: This trigger refers to a change to a
        Requirement that impacts an existing plan.  For example, a
        change of the position of the target of the Requirement.
    :ivar requirement_timing: This trigger a Requirement that is not
        expected to meet its timing constraints.
    :ivar zone_violation: This trigger refers to an OpZone conflicts
        with the current plan.
    :ivar orbit_conflict: This trigger refers to the position along a
        future planned/predicted/propagated orbit for a spacecraft
        exceeding a minimum geospatial separation limit with another
        item or items.
    :ivar off_planned_orbit: This trigger refers to a spacecraft that
        has deviated from its planned orbit to such a degree that a
        replan is required.
    :ivar spacecraft_endurance_low: This trigger refers to a low
        remaining endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power.
        This trigger can further be specialized by setting trigger
        thresholds in descendant elements.
    :ivar spacecraft_proximity_conflict: This trigger refers to the
        proximity of two spacecraft (Systems, Entities or other space
        items) that exceeded a minimum geospatial separation limit.
        Monitoring for this trigger should be based on current position
        of live items, not planned/predicted/propagated positions of
        Systems; see sibling OrbitConflict element.
    :ivar response_id: This trigger indicates planning triggered by a
        Response and/or ResponsePlan.
    """

    capability_added: None | CapabilityTaxonomyType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "CapabilityAdded",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
