@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class AmtiActivityCommandType(RfSharedApertureActivityCommandBaseType):
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar attempt: If specified, indicates the specific attempt of an
        activity to which this command applies.
    :ivar change_dependent_activity: Changes Activities that this
        Activity is dependent on.  If the dependent Activity's Resource
        Allocation is removed or never allocated, this Activity's
        Resource Allocation will be removed or not fulfilled.  This is
        used to tie Activities within or across subsystems.
    :ivar resource_selection: Indicates the unique ID of a Shared
        Antenna and/or AntennaResources to be used for the resulting
        Activity. This allows Mission Processing to direct an specific
        antenna, antenna resource type, or antenna resource instance to
        be used by the resulting Activity.
    :ivar target_volume: Indicates the volume or specific Entity that
        defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the
        command. For VOLUME AMTI Capabilities, the entity is not an
        option. For CUED AMTI Capabilities, two instances of this
        element are allowed to support an air volume that defines the
        extents of the cue volume around the Entity. For CUED AMTI
        Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in
        which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents
        of the cue volume or a sensor volume with a cue velocity. For
        TRACK AMTI Capabilities it is expected that the Entity is the
        only valid selection.
    :ivar blanking_volume: Indicates an air volume that should be
        "blanked"; the Capability should not generate outputs associated
        with the volume because it is a known source of clutter or other
        interference for the Capability. For example, a blanking volume
        could be created around a wind farm that interferes with AMTI.
    :ivar frequency: Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command.
        If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient
        within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand,
        MDF, etc.
    :ivar collection_options: Indicates guidance regarding which aspect
        or aspects of collection to favor if the command cannot be
        optimally scheduled as requested.
    :ivar collection_constraints: Indicates a set of bounding
        requirements for the particular collection associated with this
        command. The subsystem should attempt to satisfy all specified
        constraints.
    :ivar tracking_range: Indicates the range within which a track
        should be initiated and a corresponding Entity message reported
        for detected moving targets. Beyond this range tracks should not
        be initiated and Entity should not be reported for detected
        moving targets. This element can be used to control track
        loading for large and/or dense search volumes. If omitted
        tracking range selection is left to discretion of the command
        recipient.
    :ivar repetition: Indicates the required repetition of the command.
        If omitted, the command should be performed once.
    :ivar product_output: Indicates a required output Product of the
        Command. Only Products consistent with AMTI and supported by the
        commanded AMTI Capability should be requested. If omitted, no
        output Product should be produced. See ProductTypeEnum for
        further details.
    """

