@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class SupportManagementRequestType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar replan: Indicates a request to replan the subject SupportPlan.
        A replan is based on the set of Requirements and constraints
        from the SupportPlanRequest message(s) that led to the
        SupportPlan.  Other data is used from "current" sources.  For
        example current supporting system availability, battlespace
        conditions and threat locations could be different than when the
        SupportPlan was created.  A replan updates the SupportPlan to
        reflect current conditions.  Note that "current" has a different
        meaning in pre-mission planning vs. live mission planning.
        Results of the replan are reported in the corresponding
        SupportPlanStatus message.
    :ivar validation: Indicates a request to validate the subject
        SupportPlan.  Results of the validation are reported in the
        corresponding SupportPlanStatus message.
    :ivar approval_response: Indicates a "request" to give an approval
        response related to the subject SupportPlan.
    :ivar activation: Indicates a request to transition the subject
        SupportPlan to the specified activation state.  Note that this
        enumerated choice can be used to request activation and
        deactivation of a SupportPlan.  Activated SupportPlans are
        stopped by deactivating them, not by cancelling them.
        SupportPlans should only be cancelled prior to activation.  Note
        that the state machine that includes cancellation is in the
        SupportPlanStatus message while the state machine for activation
        state is in the SupportPlanExecutionStatus.
    :ivar cancel_requirement: Indicates a request to cancel a
        Requirement which has been allocated and planned when a replan
        to deallocate the Requirement isn't possible or can't be
        initiated by the cancelling actor.  This request is analogous to
        the  [Requirement]CancelCommand* messages used in non-Support
        use cases.  This request should result in the Requirement being
        canceled unless execution was already inevitable.  If the
        Requirement was inevitable and started executing but can be
        stopped (such as a long imagery collection) it should cancel as
        soon as possible, prior to completion.  Cancelling a Requirement
        doesn't necessarily trigger a replan, therefore a System could
        continue to navigate routes related to the canceled Requirement,
        even though the Requirement won't occur.  A subsequent replan
        could exclude the Requirement.  Status or feedback for this
        request is given through SupportManagementRequestStatus but the
        resulting status of the Requirement is given through
        [Requirement]Status messages.
    """

    replan: None | SupportReplanRequestType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "Replan",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    validation: None | SupportValidationRequestType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "Validation",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    approval_response: None | SupportApprovalResponseType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "ApprovalResponse",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    activation: None | SupportPlanActivationRequestEnum = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "Activation",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
    cancel_requirement: None | RequirementInstanceIdChoiceType = field(
        default=None,
        metadata={
            "name": "CancelRequirement",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )


