@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductProcessingRequestMdt(RequestBaseType):
    """
    See annotations in child elements and associated global element
    (message) for further details.

    :ivar function_id: Indicates the unique ID of this processing
        Function. At least one of FunctionID, SystemID, or ServiceID
        needs to be specified in order to uniquely identify what is
        performing the processing.
    :ivar system_id: Indicates the unique ID of this processing System.
        At least one of FunctionID, SystemID, or ServiceID needs to be
        specified in order to uniquely identify what is performing the
        processing.
    :ivar capability_id: Indicates the Capability that generated the
        product - NOT the processing Capability.  This element can be a
        useful for addressing a processing request to a specific
        instance of a Capability controller interface for reprocessing
        of a product by the Capability's host Subsystem.
    :ivar service_id: Indicates the unique ID of this processing System.
        At least one of FunctionID, SystemID, or ServiceID needs to be
        specified in order to uniquely identify what is performing the
        processing.
    :ivar traceability: The traceability element is included in this
        message as a pass through for population of the resulting
        product metadata. Tasking sources work at different levels of
        detail and abstraction, progressing from what to do to how
        specifically to do it.  Inputs from abstract tasking sources and
        Tasks can be decomposed into discrete, actionable Tasks.  This
        element provides traceability to the external tasking or Task
        from which this Task was derived.
    :ivar rank: Indicates the rank of the resulting action.  Rank
        determines order when resources are limited.
    :ivar preempt_lower_rank: Indicates whether a) in-work activities of
        a lower rank should be interrupted in order to immediately
        commence new activity (IMMEDIATE) or b) the activity should be
        simply queued according to rank and await the next available
        slot.
    :ivar processing_requirements: A processing requirement specifies
        the product to process and what processing type and processing
        parameters to utilize. If the ProductProcessing element is
        omitted, the request would imply utilization of the Product
        Processing Plan in making the determination of processing type
        and parameters.  Each processing requirement specifies one and
        only one processing "job" or call to a processing algorithm.
    """

