@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationPlan(ProductOrFileClassificationPlanMt):
    """
    This message indicates the default system rules for determining at
    which classification a product or file should be labeled.

    Classification labeling can happen in 3 ways. 1.) Classification is
    specified as part of the collection task. This method is used to tell
    the sensor subsystem to label the product or file with classification
    as part of product or file creation. When this method is used, the
    Product Or File Classification Plan can be used to determine the
    classification of the collection task based on the filter criteria such
    as zone or time. 2.) The operator creates a Product Or File
    Classification Task to perform post-collect, post-download
    classification (or reclassification) of a product or file. With this
    method, the operator can choose to classify based on the Product Or
    File Classification Plan or can override the plan by specifying a
    classification. 3.) The classification of a product generated from
    product processing does not directly use this plan to determine
    classification. The default behavior would be for the processing
    function to classify the new product with the highest classification of
    the new product's parent products. The operator has the ability to
    override this default behavior using the ProcessingTask and
    ProcessingRequest messages. If any post-creation
    classification/reclassification of processed products is desired,
    method 2 described above should be utilized. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


