@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationReport(ProductOrFileClassificationReportMt):
    """
    This message provides a report of the classification of a product or
    file.

    It has 2 primary uses: 1.) To report (via publish/broadcast) the state
    of a product or file classification. This is primarily for operator SA
    and is extremely useful for providing insight into dynamic
    classification such as changes of streaming products. For example, a
    change in classification of an EOIR stream resulting from a Product Or
    File Classification Plan zone transition. 2.) For persistence of state
    to support initialization and recovery of a service that is applying
    security labels to products or files. This allows for a service to
    retrieve the classification label of a product or file upon
    initialization. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationRequest(ProductOrFileClassificationRequestMt):
    """
    This message has 2 uses.

    Message use 1: This message is a request that a product or file be
    classified at a particular level. A Product Or File Classification
    Request directly invokes classification service functionality to
    classify/reclassify a product or file. Execution of the classification
    request would result in a Product Or File Classification Request Status
    followed by a Product Or File Classification Report. There are 2 ways
    this message can be generated. 1.) By the operator to command immediate
    reclassification of a product or file. 2.) Automated by a service as a
    result of execution of a Classification Task. When specifying a
    Classification Request, the user can choose to utilize the Product or
    File Classification Plan to determine classification or can override
    the plan by specifying a classification. If automatically generated as
    a result of Classification Task execution, the classification
    requirements would be populated with those specified in the
    Classification Task. This allows the default plan to be utilized or
    overridden on a task by task basis. Message use 2: This message
    requests that a classification label is generated per the Product Or
    File Classification Plan and returned in the Product Or File
    Classification Request Status. When the message is used in this way,
    the classification should be omitted from the Classification
    Requirements. This message use allows for a service decomposition where
    the service applying the classification label is separate from the
    service that determines classification based on the classification
    plan. UCI_PRIMITIVE: ActionRequest-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationRequestStatusMt(MessageType):
    """
    See the associated global element (message) annotation for further
    details.

    :ivar message_data: See annotations in child elements for details.
    """

    class Meta:
        name = "ProductOrFileClassificationRequestStatusMT"

    message_data: ProductOrFileClassificationRequestStatusMdt = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "MessageData",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        }
    )


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationTask(ProductOrFileClassificationTaskMt):
    """
    This message represents a task for a product or file to be classified
    at a particular level.

    Classification Tasks do not directly invoke functionality. They are
    utilized to schedule post-collection and post-download
    classification/reclassification of products or files. As a result, it
    is expected that a Product Or File Classification Task would typically
    specify a download and/or collection task as a preceding dependent
    task. Execution of a Classification Task would result in issue of a
    Classification Request to invoke classification service functionality.
    When specifying a Classification Task, the user can choose to utilize
    the Product Or File Classification Plan to determine classification or
    can override the plan by specifying a classification. This allows the
    default plan to be overridden on a Task by Task basis. UCI_PRIMITIVE:
    Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileClassificationTaskStatus(
    ProductOrFileClassificationTaskStatusMt
):
    """
    This message provides the status of a Classification Task.

    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Status-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileDisseminationReport(ProductOrFileDisseminationReportMt):
    """
    This message provides a report of the dissemination of a product or
    file.

    It has 2 primary uses: 1.) To report (via publish/broadcast) the state
    of product or file dissemination. This is primarily for operator SA and
    is extremely useful for providing insight into dynamic dissemination
    destination changes of streaming products. For example, a change in
    dissemination destination of an EOIR stream resulting from a Product Or
    File Dissemination Plan zone transition. 2.) For persistence of state
    to support initialization and recovery of a service that is performing
    product or file dissemination. This allows for a service to retrieve
    the dissemination destination of a product or file upon initialization.
    This is primarily applicable to streaming products that are
    continuously streaming to a dissemination destination. UCI_PRIMITIVE:
    Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileDisseminationRequest(ProductOrFileDisseminationRequestMt):
    """
    This message is a request that a product or file be disseminated to one
    or more destinations.

    A Product Or File Dissemination Request directly invokes dissemination
    service functionality to disseminate a product or file. Execution of
    the dissemination request would result in a Product Or File
    Dissemination Request Status followed by a Product Or File
    Dissemination Report. There are 2 ways this message can be generated.
    1.) By the operator to command immediate dissemination of a product or
    file. 2.) Automated by a service as a result of execution of a
    Dissemination Task. When specifying a Dissemination Request, the user
    can choose to utilize the Product Or File Dissemination Plan to
    determine destination or can override the plan by specifying a
    destination. If automatically generated as a result of Dissemination
    Task execution, the Dissemination requirements would be populated with
    those specified in the Dissemination Task. This allows the default plan
    to be utilized or overridden on a task by task basis. UCI_PRIMITIVE:
    ActionRequest-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ProductOrFileDisseminationTask(ProductOrFileDisseminationTaskMt):
    """
    This message is a task for a product or file to be disseminated to one
    or more destinations.

    Dissemination Tasks do not directly invoke functionality. They can be
    utilized to schedule post-collection, post-download, and
    post-processing dissemination of products. As a result, it is expected
    that a Product Or File Dissemination Task would typically specify a
    download and/or processing task as a preceding dependent task.
    Execution of a Dissemination Task would result in issue of a
    Dissemination Request to invoke dissemination service functionality.
    When specifying a Dissemination Task, the user can choose to utilize
    the Product Or File Dissemination Plan to determine the dissemination
    destination or can override the plan by specifying a destination. This
    allows the default plan to be overridden on a task by task basis.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


