@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class DigitalResourceDefinitionType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar resource_request_option_index: Allows the resource manager to
        select a single identifier when presented with several options
        from which to pick an allocation. The requesting function
        defines the indices at the time of the request, numbering them
        1, 2, 3, etc. The ResourceAllocator responds with an allocation
        which includes the chosen index.
    :ivar stream_index: Reference to a specific usage of a
        DigitalThreadInstanceIndex, assigned by ResourceAllocator at
        allocation time. Multiple streams may be required, such as for
        separate transmit and receive streams.
    :ivar vas_endpoint: Index/Stream of the Virtual Aperture Scheduler
        (VAS) for the Service to use to address schedule requests
        (either a system level VAS or a MFA VAS). Defined in Shared
        Aperture Information Files.
    :ivar resource_access_priority: This is the priority for resource
        access where higher value is the higher priority.  Allocates the
        minimum and maximum weighted priority value in the Resource
        Access Priority range.  If the Resource Access Priority range is
        actually a discrete single weighted priority, the Min element
        and the sibling Max element should be equal.
    :ivar blanking_limit: Only present for Transmit allocations.
        Identifies the allowed blanking of the access by other
        functions. The overall blanking limit is allocated across
        Receive functions that can blank the Transmit, identified either
        by Subsystem (such as an ESM Subsystem) or a DigitalPayload
        function in either MFP or MFA.
    :ivar period_access_allocations: The allocated percent access limit
        is expected to not be exceeded by the payload. The Expected
        access alerts the Digital Payload that the scheduled accesses
        have some likelihood of meeting or not meeting the desired duty
        cycle, based on the other Activities with allocations at the
        time of the request. Actual access allocation is not known until
        schedule time (and may be interrupted by low latency events).
    :ivar pointing_vector: The effective pointing available (Field of
        Regard) of the aperture allocation.
    """

    resource_request_option_index: int = field(
        metadata={
            "name": "ResourceRequestOptionIndex",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        }
    )
    stream_index: list[int] = field(
        default_factory=list,
        metadata={
            "name": "StreamIndex",
            "type": "Element",
            "namespace": "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam",
        },
    )
