@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class AuthorizationDetailsType:
    """
    See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this
    type for details.

    :ivar system_id: Indicates the unique ID of the System which the
        sibling User is requesting or is authorized to use.
    :ivar user: Indicates Operator(s)/users that are a source of
        Requirements, described in sibling elements, for the
        Authorization.
    :ivar requirement_type: Indicates which Requirement types are being
        authorized or requested.  If omitted, the request or
        authorization applies to all Requirement types.
    :ivar requirement_usage: Indicates a requested or authorized usage
        for the sibling authorized RequirementType(s). List size for
        this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.
    :ivar rank: Indicates the highest Requirement ranking value the User
        is authorized for.
    :ivar authorized_time: This element indicates the time range during
        which the Authorization applies or is requested.  More
        specifically, this is the time range in which the User must
        create/submit Tasks in order for them to be allocated to the
        specified System.  If omitted, the Authorization is applicable
        or requested until removed.
    :ivar authorized_area: This element indicates the area over which
        the authorization applies or is requested.  More specifically,
        this is the geospatial zone in which the Requirement object must
        fall in order for the authorization to apply.  If omitted, the
        Authorization is applicable or requested to all areas.
    """

