@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ActivityPlan(ActivityPlanMt):
    """
    This message specifies planned *Capability-related activities for a
    System, independent of System kinematics.

    Activities are the planned implementation details of Effects, Actions,
    Tasks, Capability Commands, etc. Activity planning can be done manually
    by operators, by an activity planning service or a combination. This
    message decouples activity planning from allocation, kinematic and
    other types of planning; the ActivityPlan of a System can be created,
    updated and approved independent of other *Plans. It enables any type
    of *Plan to be a constraint on activity planning. An ActivityPlan can
    be an input and/or output of planning processes. For example an
    ActivityPlan from a previous round of planning could be an input to an
    activity planning service that adds additional planned activities to
    it. A single System can have multiple independent ActivityPlans for
    different Task, Capability, sensor, etc. types; that are developed by
    one or more services across a multi-System service oriented
    architecture; at different times then independently updated and
    approved. Optionally, all types of activities for a System can be
    included in a single ActivityPlan. An ActivityPlan can be created
    discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans. An
    ActivityPlan can only be activated and executed as part of a
    MissionPlan. A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of
    multiple ActivityPlans and *Plans in general. An ActivityPlan can be
    subject to approval per Approval* messages. Planning, approval,
    activation and execution state information for an ActivityPlan are
    given in other ActivityPlan* messages. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ActivityPlanCommand(ActivityPlanCommandMt):
    """
    This message commands an ActivityPlan related planning function/action.

    Example planning functions include updating an existing ActivityPlan,
    creating a new ActivityPlan or combining/stitching existing
    ActivityPlans together. The command includes many inputs to the
    planning function while others may come from a variety of other
    messages. The expected output of the planning function is an
    ActivityPlan message. The command includes options for constraining the
    planning function in a variety of ways using existing plans of the same
    type or by other plan types. For example, an ActivityPlan could be
    constrained by a previous ActivityPlan and/or a TaskPlan. The command
    includes environment overrides to selectively modify details of the
    current planning environment in the context of a single planning
    command. For example, a known threat Entity in the environment could be
    removed and an expected Entity could be for added to the environment in
    the context of a single planning command in support of speculative or
    "what-if" contingency planning. The command includes settings for
    "weightings" that influence the decisions of operators or planning
    algorithms performing the planning. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


