@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OrbitActivityPlan(OrbitActivityPlanMt):
    """
    This message specifies planned activities for a System with an
    OrbitPlan.

    An "Orbit Activity" is any *Capability-related activity planned in
    context of the kinematic OrbitPlan of the System. Activities are the
    planned implementation details of Effects, Actions, Tasks, Capability
    Commands, etc. Orbit activity planning can be done manually by
    operators, by an activity planning service or a combination. This
    message decouples activity planning from allocation, kinematic and
    other types of planning; the OrbitActivityPlan of a System can be
    created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans. It enables
    any type of *Plan to be a constraint on activity planning. An
    OrbitActivityPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes.
    For example an OrbitActivityPlan from a previous round of planning
    could be an input to an activity planning service that adds additional
    planned activities to it. A single System can have multiple independent
    OrbitActivityPlans for different Task, Capability, sensor, etc. types;
    that are developed by one or more services across a multi-System
    service oriented architecture; at different times then independently
    updated and approved. Optionally, all types of activities for a System
    can be included in a single OrbitActivityPlan. An OrbitActivityPlan can
    be created discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other
    *Plans. An OrbitActivityPlan can only be activated and executed as part
    of a MissionPlan. A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order
    of multiple OrbitActivityPlans and *Plans in general. An
    OrbitActivityPlan can be subject to approval per Approval* messages.
    Planning, approval, activation and execution state information for an
    OrbitActivityPlan are given in other OrbitActivityPlan* messages.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OrbitActivityPlanCommand(OrbitActivityPlanCommandMt):
    """
    This message invokes an OrbitActivityPlan planning process.

    Each planning process is declared with a unique ID in the ControlStatus
    message; that ID is used in this message to invoke the process. The
    message includes many inputs to the planning process but many others
    may come from a variety of other messages. A few examples of the many
    inputs include: 1. Options for constraining the planning function in a
    variety of ways using existing Plans of the same type or by other Plan
    types. For example, an OrbitActivityPlan could be constrained by an
    existing kinematic OrbitPlan, a previous OrbitActivityPlan and/or a
    TaskPlan. 2. Environment overrides to selectively modify details of the
    current planning environment in the context of a single planning
    command. For example, a known threat Entity in the environment could be
    removed and an expected Entity could be for added to the environment in
    the context of a single planning command in support of "what-if"
    planning. 3. "Weightings" that influence the decisions of operators or
    planning algorithms performing the planning. 4. Temporal and/or
    kinematic begin and end points. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class OrbitPlan(OrbitPlanMt):
    """
    This message specifies the planned kinematic details of a particular
    System's orbit; "orbit" is defined as a series of orbital element sets,
    ephemeris, vector covariance and/or explicit maneuvers between them.

    The message is intended for Systems such as spacecraft whose kinematic
    plans are best represented in inertial/orbital frames. Orbit planning
    can be done manually by operators, by a route planning service or a
    combination. This message decouples kinematic planning from allocation,
    action and other types of planning; the kinematic OrbitPlan of a System
    can be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans. It
    enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on route planning. An
    OrbitPlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes. For
    example a coarse OrbitPlan created by the top System in a hierarchical
    System of System for overall Mission orchestration and deconfliction
    could be an input to a orbit planning service that the produces a
    detailed, executable OrbitPlan for a specific subordinate System. A
    single System can have multiple independent OrbitPlans for different
    orbit planning considerations such as orbit station keeping, orbital
    maneuvers and attitude adjustment. The different planning
    considerations can be handled by one or more services across a
    multi-System service oriented architecture at different times then
    independently updated and approved. Optionally, all kinematic orbit
    planning considerations for a System can be included in a single
    OrbitPlan. An OrbitPlan can be created discretely or as part of a
    MissionPlan that includes other *Plans. An OrbitPlan can only be
    activated and executed as part of a MissionPlan. A MissionPlan can be
    used to plan the execution order of multiple OrbitPlans and *Plans in
    general. An OrbitPlan can be subject to approval per Approval*
    messages. Planning, approval, activation and execution state
    information for an OrbitPlan are given in other OrbitPlan* messages.
    UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


