@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class SupportRequest(SupportRequestMt):
    """
    This message is a Direct C2 request for support from an "external"
    supporting asset.

    The supported asset to supporting asset relationship could be any
    combination of peer-to-peer, cross-domain, cross-C2-hierarchy,
    cross-combatant command, joint, coalition, cross-classification, etc.
    The taxonomy for UCI Support C2 is the same as the UCI taxonomy for
    Planned C2, Response C2 and Direct C2. All four use the same set of
    "verbs" described in the Effect, Action, Task, Response and
    [Capability]Command messages. SupportRequests include two kinds of
    "actors": requesting/supported system, responding/supporting system.
    See annotations for associated elements for cardinality and details.
    UCI Support C2 includes planned and direct options. The UCI
    SupportRequest* messages require a supported asset to have minimal
    apriori knowledge of the supporting asset and vice-versa as compared to
    UCI MissionPlan* and related messages. UCI_PRIMITIVE: ActionRequest-2.
    """

