@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ResponsePlan(ResponsePlanMt):
    """
    This message specifies the Responses allocated to a System.

    Allocation can be done manually by operators, by an allocation service
    or a combination. This message decouples Response allocation from
    kinematic, action and other types of planning; Response allocations can
    be created, updated and approved independent of other *Plans. It
    enables any type of *Plan to be a constraint on Response allocation. A
    ResponsePlan can be an input and/or output of planning processes. For
    example the ResponsePlan for the top System in a hierarchical System of
    System could be an input to a response allocation service that the
    produces a ResponsePlan per subordinate System with their subset of
    allocated Responses. Additional details such as timing, dependencies,
    decomposition, etc. can be added during the response allocation process
    and captured in the ResponsePlan to supplement the information in the
    allocated Responses themselves. A ResponsePlan can be created
    discretely or as part of a MissionPlan that includes other *Plans. A
    ResponsePlan can only be activated and executed as part of a
    MissionPlan. A MissionPlan can be used to plan the execution order of
    multiple ResponsePlans and *Plans in general. A ResponsePlan can be
    subject to approval per Approval* messages. Planning, approval,
    activation and execution state information for a ResponsePlan are given
    in other ResponsePlan* messages. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class ResponsePlanCommand(ResponsePlanCommandMt):
    """
    This message indicates a command to perform a response allocation plan
    process or function.

    The ResponsePlan message/object is the output of a response allocation
    plan process or function. The ResponsePlan output of one response
    allocation plan process function could be an input to the next
    function. UCI enables "discovery" of the response allocation plan
    processes and functions of a System via the ControlStatus message. This
    mechanism for discovery empowers a System performing response
    allocation planning for subordinate Systems of heterogeneous types
    and/or service/function/process architecture to selectively use,
    replace or supplement them. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


