@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class MissionPlan(MissionPlanMt):
    """
    This message specifies an integrated set of sub-*Plans (TaskPlan,
    RoutePlan and RouteActivityPlan for example) that together are the
    mission plan for a single System.

    Mission planning can be done manually by operators, by planning
    services or a combination. This message references a set of coherent
    sub-*Plans and indicates the order in which they will be executed when
    activated. The sub-*Plans can be discretely created then integrated
    into the MissionPlan or created near simultaneously in a single or
    multiple step mission planning process that creates all sub-*Plans. A
    MissionPlan can be created, updated and approved somewhat independent
    of its sub-*Plans. For a hierarchical System of Systems, a higher
    tiered System's MissionPlan can reference the related/coherent
    MissionPlans of subordinate Systems. *Plans can only be activated and
    executed as part of a MissionPlan. A MissionPlan can be subject to
    approval per Approval* messages. Planning, approval, activation and
    execution state information for a MissionPlan are given in other
    MissionPlan* messages. UCI_PRIMITIVE: Data-1.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


@dataclass(kw_only=True)
class MissionPlanCommand(MissionPlanCommandMt):
    """
    This message invokes a MissionPlan planning process.

    Each planning process is declared with a unique ID in the ControlStatus
    message; that ID is used in this message to invoke the process. A
    MissionPlan is an aggregation of other *Plan types, therefore
    MissionPlanCommand planning processes (and this message) can result in
    multiple *Plan types/messages. This message includes many inputs to the
    planning process but many others may come from a variety of other
    messages. A few examples of the many inputs include: 1. Options for
    constraining the planning function in a variety of ways using existing
    Plans of the same type or by other Plan types. For example, a
    MissionPlan could be constrained by a previous RoutePlan, a previous
    RouteActivityPlan and/or a TaskPlan. 2. Environment overrides to
    selectively modify details of the current planning environment in the
    context of a single planning command. For example, a known threat
    Entity in the environment could be removed and an expected Entity could
    be added to the environment in the context of a single planning command
    in support of "what-if" planning. 3. "Weightings" that influence the
    decisions of operators or planning algorithms performing the planning.
    4. Temporal and/or kinematic begin and end points. UCI_PRIMITIVE:
    Command-2.
    """

    class Meta:
        namespace = "https://www.vdl.afrl.af.mil/programs/oam"


